{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess","id":1452119,"title":"Let's talk about the Charms of ExEss","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-13T23:23:38-07:00","id":1452119,"title":"Let's talk about the Charms of ExEss","content":"I think it's appropriate to have a specific topic for this one.<br /> <br /> I like most of the Charms that have been published, but I'll start my first post by talking about the ones I don't like actually, don't let that make you think I'm negative about the upcoming game. These are Charms that either create more rolls when it's not necessary (to me), or that I don't think players will have a real use of because the situation rarely happens (at least in my games), or because I feel there is a sort of contradiction with the base system (the effect seems good reading it, but the system doesn't seem to actually make it good). Maybe some people will show me good reasons on why this Charm was design like this and make me change my mind about it. I understand that the devs made these decisions intentionally most of the time, I just probably don't understand their intentions.<br /> <br /> <b>Flickering Shadow Evasion (and it's Close Combat counterpart)</b><br /> <br /> &quot;On Step 4, roll your choice of Attribute + Athletics, and add your successes to your Defense against the attack.&quot; I really don't like rolling for defense, I thought that 3e did the good choice by removing rolls for defense. I think any option like &quot;Add Ability do your Defense&quot; would be as effective and less annoying<br /> <br /> <b>Efficient Crafting Technique</b><br /> <br /> In particular, I don't understand the Solar mode : At Essence 2, the Solar waives all penalties from inappropriate tools or workspace (upgrade from negate 3 penalties). From my understanding -3 is the biggest environnemental/external penalty you can have (corresponding to some kind of Yozi curse for example), and they don't stack. I'm really unsure what this mode is for.<br /> <br /> <b>Strange Tongue Understanding </b><br /> <br /> The base effect &quot;Their understanding is not sophisticated, however. They get by with minimal reading and speech in a foreign tongue without needing to roll, but complex discussion or literature requires an Embassy roll at default difficulty.&quot; seems good on paper, but if I try to imagine a scene where this comes on I don't think it's actually appropriate. If you can actually just understand foreign tongues with an Embassy rolls, and complex discussions are at Default Difficulty (meaning 3 to me), the actual character would success understanding a basic conversation with any Embassy roll, and I don't get what this Charm is for. There is another specific mechanical bonus on this Charm after that seems good though, but it's &quot;core effect&quot; seems to not really work mechanically to me<br /> <br /> <b>Stubborn Boar Defense</b><br /> <br /> I don't usually spam my PC's with the same social influence effect when it has failed once as it seems a bit repetitive, or at least I don't do it again during the same session. This really doesn't seem useful for my players. Do you guys have regular occurence where this Charm would be useful ? I'm genuinely curious<br /> <br /> <b>Memetic Dogma Discipline </b><br /> <br /> I don't usually use rolls between my NPC's to make them convince each other, as the social system is not as &quot;basic&quot; as the DD one, considering you have to account for Intimacies, Virtues, repurhase of social influence, etc ... This could arguably have some effect on other PC's but I feel like this is a bit niche. I think I understand the intended purpose of the Charm, but mechanically I really don't feel like someone at my table is gonna have use of this Charm. I would have preferred something like a Venture to spread ideas through Performance, or directly &quot;Any person in contact with the initial spectators will form a temporary Minor Intimacy towards the Exalt's ideas or make a Hard Bargain&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Essence-Lending Method </b><br /> <br /> &quot;Essence Font Technique (Solar): Roll Finesse + Lore against difficulty 3. On success, the Exalt generates three additional motes which may be transferred to the target in place of their own. These motes dissipate immediately if not transferred.&quot; Depending on wether you actually need to pay at least 1 mote for the Charm to function, this feels like a possible &quot;infinite mote for my allies&quot; shenanigan<br /> <br /> <b>Cunning Warrior Regimen</b><br /> <br /> I genuinely can't tell what the difference is between this Charm and League of Iron Preparation.<br /> <br /> As a thing that bothers me a little, I notice a lot of the Social Charms have effects like &quot;For the rest of the scene, gain +1 success on rolls to ...&quot; or &quot;For the rest of the scene, gain 1 resolve to ...&quot; which I don't like for the same reasons that I don't like these Charms in 3e (dice adders). I guess this design comes from the fact that Exalts don't regen motes outside of combat quickly, and they noticed that without Charms like this anyone who is not a Solar for excellencies would quickly have 0 possible way to augment his rolls in any action scene past the first few rolls","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T11:08:23-07:00","id":1452184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess#post1452119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Flickering Shadow Evasion (and it's Close Combat counterpart)</b><br /> <br /> &quot;On Step 4, roll your choice of Attribute + Athletics, and add your successes to your Defense against the attack.&quot; I really don't like rolling for defense, I thought that 3e did the good choice by removing rolls for defense. I think any option like &quot;Add Ability do your Defense&quot; would be as effective and less annoying</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but Essence definitely isn't opposed to having a lot of steps involved in things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Efficient Crafting Technique</b><br /> <br /> In particular, I don't understand the Solar mode : At Essence 2, the Solar waives all penalties from inappropriate tools or workspace (upgrade from negate 3 penalties). From my understanding -3 is the biggest environnemental/external penalty you can have (corresponding to some kind of Yozi curse for example), and they don't stack. I'm really unsure what this mode is for. </div> </div> </div>I have no idea. That seems like a version thing, so I'm reporting it for errata.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Strange Tongue Understanding </b><br /> <br /> The base effect &quot;Their understanding is not sophisticated, however. They get by with minimal reading and speech in a foreign tongue without needing to roll, but complex discussion or literature requires an Embassy roll at default difficulty.&quot; seems good on paper, but if I try to imagine a scene where this comes on I don't think it's actually appropriate. If you can actually just understand foreign tongues with an Embassy rolls, and complex discussions are at Default Difficulty (meaning 3 to me), the actual character would success understanding a basic conversation with any Embassy roll, and I don't get what this Charm is for. There is another specific mechanical bonus on this Charm after that seems good though, but it's &quot;core effect&quot; seems to not really work mechanically to me </div> </div> </div>I think that's mostly flavor text, but it could also lead to some roleplaying wrinkles. The odd thing to me is that, rules-wise, an &quot;unsophisticated&quot; understanding of a language does nothing to impede your own actions, but does make you resistant to influence. Then, if you buy the upgrade, your &quot;better&quot; grasp on the language takes away that bonus, and does give you a penalty - in fact, two-success penalty, which is actually worse than the three-die penalty for being cursed by the Yozis themselves.<br /> <br /> Nothing suggests that you take that penalty if you succeed at the Embassy roll to use the Charm <i>without</i> the upgrade, nor that you can waive the upgrade once you've bought it.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm getting at, I like the idea behind the limitation, but think the mechanics are, at best, not described very clearly - surely the intention is that you take a penalty to actions with the first version, too, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Stubborn Boar Defense</b><br /> <br /> I don't usually spam my PC's with the same social influence effect when it has failed once as it seems a bit repetitive, or at least I don't do it again during the same session. This really doesn't seem useful for my players. Do you guys have regular occurence where this Charm would be useful ? I'm genuinely curious </div> </div> </div>This is a little tricky. &quot;Keep spamming the same influence action over and over&quot; is a classic abusive tactic in many influence systems, so having an answer for that isn't crazy... but doesn't it make more sense as a general rule that something you have to not only buy as a Charm, but also spend two motes on? Even without accounting for the apparent ease of ignoring influence in EE, that's a really steep buy-in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Memetic Dogma Discipline </b><br /> <br /> I don't usually use rolls between my NPC's to make them convince each other, as the social system is not as &quot;basic&quot; as the DD one, considering you have to account for Intimacies, Virtues, repurhase of social influence, etc ... This could arguably have some effect on other PC's but I feel like this is a bit niche. I think I understand the intended purpose of the Charm, but mechanically I really don't feel like someone at my table is gonna have use of this Charm. I would have preferred something like a Venture to spread ideas through Performance, or directly &quot;Any person in contact with the initial spectators will form a temporary Minor Intimacy towards the Exalt's ideas or make a Hard Bargain&quot; </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the only clear use I see for this is to double dip on Teamwork effects for an ally, which is probably not a great place to be. I do really like the idea of creating a specialized Venture, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Essence-Lending Method </b><br /> <br /> &quot;Essence Font Technique (Solar): Roll Finesse + Lore against difficulty 3. On success, the Exalt generates three additional motes which may be transferred to the target in place of their own. These motes dissipate immediately if not transferred.&quot; Depending on wether you actually need to pay at least 1 mote for the Charm to function, this feels like a possible &quot;infinite mote for my allies&quot; shenanigan </div> </div> </div>Yikes. I hadn't thought of that, but I had noticed that two Solars with this Charm can pretty easily go infinite (which also extends to the rest of the group). I think that must be an oversight, and am reporting it for errata.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Cunning Warrior Regimen</b><br /> <br /> I genuinely can't tell what the difference is between this Charm and League of Iron Preparation. </div> </div> </div>Hard to say until we get to Antagonists. LoIP makes noncombatants into &quot;Conscripts,&quot; which might be better than some lesser statblock? It also gives them Regular Drill, and can eventually upgrade them to an even-better statblock. CWR does one thing and one thing only: increase the Outnumber quality, whatever that means.<br /> <br /> This is, admittedly, made muddier by LoIP <i>also</i> being able to increase Outnumber, possibly without an upper limit. Definitely something to try and double-check once we know more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a thing that bothers me a little, I notice a lot of the Social Charms have effects like &quot;For the rest of the scene, gain +1 success on rolls to ...&quot; or &quot;For the rest of the scene, gain 1 resolve to ...&quot; which I don't like for the same reasons that I don't like these Charms in 3e (dice adders). I guess this design comes from the fact that Exalts don't regen motes outside of combat quickly, and they noticed that without Charms like this anyone who is not a Solar for excellencies would quickly have 0 possible way to augment his rolls in any action scene past the first few rolls </div> </div> </div>I can see that - Second Chance Approach and Dread Tiger's Symmetry at least incentivize specific types of action, but Harmonious Presence Methodology in particular just adds dice to everything. At that point, it seems like it could be &quot;Commit 1 mote, get free social Excellencies for the scene,&quot; to keep thing s streamlined (with a really sweet Solar mode to make up for the base effect being useless to them).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T12:05:20-07:00","id":1452195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452184#post1452184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, but Essence definitely isn't opposed to having a lot of steps involved in things.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say there is a difference between having lots of steps and rolling a lot of steps <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that's mostly flavor text, but it could also lead to some roleplaying wrinkles. The odd thing to me is that, rules-wise, an &quot;unsophisticated&quot; understanding of a language does nothing to impede your own actions, but does make you resistant to influence. Then, if you buy the upgrade, your &quot;better&quot; grasp on the language takes away that bonus, and does give you a penalty - in fact, two-success penalty, which is actually worse than the three-die penalty for being cursed by the Yozis themselves.<br /> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is flavor text because the flavor text actually includes a mechanical description at the end of the sentence. I don't believe they usually do this with flavor text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a little tricky. &quot;Keep spamming the same influence action over and over&quot; is a classic abusive tactic in many influence systems, so having an answer for that isn't crazy... but doesn't it make more sense as a general rule that something you have to not only buy as a Charm, but also spend two motes on? Even without accounting for the apparent ease of ignoring influence in EE, that's a really steep buy-in. </div> </div> </div>I didn't think it could serve against abuse. Hopefully that makes it really useless at my table because I won't bully my players then !<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, the only clear use I see for this is to double dip on Teamwork effects for an ally, which is probably not a great place to be. I do really like the idea of creating a specialized Venture, though. </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly suprised I see so few Venture-creating actions in Charms (only in War I think). This is probably their greatest design idea in ExEss so far, which answers most of the problems I've had mastering Ex3 and that the system had no answer for, but I feel like they don't use it to its full potential by not interacting that much with Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yikes. I hadn't thought of that, but I had noticed that two Solars with this Charm can pretty easily go infinite (which also extends to the rest of the group). I think that must be an oversight, and am reporting it for errata. </div> </div> </div>I'm unsure they consider these kinds of things as errata, though. They seem very adamant that a lot of balance questions are design decisions, not errors they are expecting backing for from us<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hard to say until we get to Antagonists. LoIP makes noncombatants into &quot;Conscripts,&quot; which might be better than some lesser statblock? It also gives them Regular Drill, and can eventually upgrade them to an even-better statblock. CWR does one thing and one thing only: increase the Outnumber quality, whatever that means.<br /> <br /> This is, admittedly, made muddier by LoIP <i>also</i> being able to increase Outnumber, possibly without an upper limit. Definitely something to try and double-check once we know more. </div> </div> </div>I mean, LoIP also makes conscript into soldiers, and can also give Outnumber Quality, and is apparently stackable (as suggested by &quot;Each benefit provided by this Charm can only be applied to a given unit once:&quot; mention). So it's possible to train soldiers to give them Outnumber Quality, not only non-combattants. If Cunning Warrior Regimen serves only to train things that are not non combattants, conscripts and soldiers over LoIP, it seems a bit niche. Especially considering that at Essence 3, LoIP can also train &quot;spirits, animals or other non-humans&quot;, so basically everything. It's as if Cunning Warrior Regimen served only for the specific feature of giving any Battlegroup an Outnumber Quality during Essence 1 and 2 because LoIP covers it at Essence 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T12:23:45-07:00","id":1452199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452195#post1452195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it is flavor text because the flavor text actually includes a mechanical description at the end of the sentence. I don't believe they usually do this with flavor text.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, in an edition with actual separated-out flavor text, that was poorly put. What I meant is that's there to inform roleplaying, and maybe sometimes have the ST say &quot;no, you cannot convey your philosophical treatise on how Oblivion is superior to reincarnation using a combination of pidgin and hand signs.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I didn't think it could serve against abuse. Hopefully that makes it really useless at my table because I won't bully my players then ! </div> </div> </div>To be clear, I meant &quot;abuse&quot; as in a tactic for getting game rules to do things they're not designed to do, not as in abusing your fellow players. That would be way worse!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm unsure they consider these kinds of things as errata, though. They seem very adamant that a lot of balance questions are design decisions, not errors they are expecting backing for from us </div> </div> </div>I am trying very hard to only file errata when a rule does not work, or I don't understand what it is trying to tell me. However, &quot;unlimited motes for the whole party all the time&quot; is such a major power level issue that I honestly believe it must be me not understanding the Charm's intention. I guess we'll find out when the backer PDF happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's as if Cunning Warrior Regimen served only for the specific feature of giving any Battlegroup an Outnumber Quality during Essence 1 and 2 because LoIP covers it at Essence 3. </div> </div> </div>Actually, you may have solved it there - it seems like we could be looking back into a version of the rules where Charms still had other Charms as prerequisites. I am not so confident of that as to submit errata, but I wouldn't be shocked if one of those becomes a repurchase of the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T12:26:44-07:00","id":1452200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess#post1452119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Efficient Crafting Technique</b><br /> <br /> In particular, I don't understand the Solar mode : At Essence 2, the Solar waives all penalties from inappropriate tools or workspace (upgrade from negate 3 penalties). From my understanding -3 is the biggest environnemental/external penalty you can have (corresponding to some kind of Yozi curse for example), and they don't stack. I'm really unsure what this mode is for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the penalty from trying to do, say, gemcutting, without any tools at all, could be very steep, and potentially better than -3. Social influence without talking is a 2-success penalty (similar to 4 dice) even with a suitable Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T12:46:46-07:00","id":1452204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452200#post1452200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the penalty from trying to do, say, gemcutting, without any tools at all, could be very steep, and potentially better than -3. Social influence without talking is a 2-success penalty (similar to 4 dice) even with a suitable Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's very little textual support for that. That social influence penalty is a pretty extreme outlier (I wonder if it was meant to be two <i>dice</i>), and the rules only let it be that bad due to coming from a Charm. &quot;Outside of Charms, a situational or environmental penalty should not exceed three,&quot; according to the Bonuses and Penalties section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T13:03:28-07:00","id":1452208,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile, in the Dragon-Blooded Charms preview: does anyone have a reasonable guess about what &quot;the Exalt must be able to make a decisive attack area of effect&quot; is trying to say?<br /> <br /> It seems like that sentence is supposed to explain the size and range of the attack (and maybe whether it applies its full Power to all targets), but I have no specific guesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T13:10:56-07:00","id":1452211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452200#post1452200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the penalty from trying to do, say, gemcutting, without any tools at all, could be very steep, and potentially better than -3. Social influence without talking is a 2-success penalty (similar to 4 dice) even with a suitable Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, even if that's the case, Charms that reduce dice penalties do not reduce success penalties I believe. And -3 is really bad, I really just don't see telling someone &quot;You wanna go some gemcutting without tools ? My poor man, it's even harder than having <i>literally woven into Fate</i> that you can't cut gems&quot;<br /> <br /> Since they put environment penalties and tool penalties in the same pool, and from what I understand (but I might be wrong) they don't stack, I just don't get how this is supposed to work","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T13:27:07-07:00","id":1452217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452208#post1452208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, in the Dragon-Blooded Charms preview: does anyone have a reasonable guess about what &quot;the Exalt must be able to make a decisive attack area of effect&quot; is trying to say?<br /> <br /> It seems like that sentence is supposed to explain the size and range of the attack (and maybe whether it applies its full Power to all targets), but I have no specific guesses.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My guess is DB are gonna have different Charms that allow them to make &quot;Decisive attack area of effect&quot;. If it is it should be clear enough","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T13:32:31-07:00","id":1452218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452217#post1452217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My guess is DB are gonna have different Charms that allow them to make &quot;Decisive attack area of effect&quot;. If it is it should be clear enough</div> </div> </div> </div>that or maybe its a weapon tag? one of the two<br /> <br /> Edit: Scratch that, got a confirm from Monica that's in the sorcery part. Said it is likely something they will move","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T13:39:03-07:00","id":1452220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452218#post1452218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> that or maybe its a weapon tag? one of the two<br /> <br /> Edit: Scratch that, got a confirm from Monica that's in the sorcery part. Said it is likely something they will move</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I just saw someone confirming this on the Discord as well, I'm really curious about it now ! <br /> <br /> Iwonder if this means that the DB will necessitate to have prepared the AoE spell to activate the Charm, or he just needs to master it and can use the Charm without having to cast the spell ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T13:53:18-07:00","id":1452225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452220#post1452220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I just saw someone confirming this on the Discord as well, I'm really curious about it now !<br /> <br /> Iwonder if this means that the DB will necessitate to have prepared the AoE spell to activate the Charm, or he just needs to master it and can use the Charm without having to cast the spell ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so.<br /> <br /> The key clue is the word <i>decisive.</i> To make a decisive attack against a single target, you need Power at least equal to their Hardness. So to make a decisive area of effect attack, how much Power do you need? Maybe the maximum Hardness of any target, or the number of targets, or something else? Whatever the answer to that question is, I'm pretty sure that the rule is contained in the Sorcery section, and that rule is what the DB Charm is referencing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T13:56:10-07:00","id":1452226,"title":"","content":"Or if &quot;able to make a decisive attack area of effect&quot; is defined as X Will, or (11 Power - Essence), or who even knows what else.<br /> <br /> It's not shocking to have orphaned rules in a sneak preview, of course, but I don't think I would have guessed that the general rules for handling any particular native Charm would be under Sorcery. I'm glad to hear that's (probably) going to move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T14:37:27-07:00","id":1452237,"title":"","content":"Someone remind me, is the Air version of Dragon-Graced Weapon in non-Essence 3e a Cold attack or a wind gust for knock back?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T14:40:20-07:00","id":1452238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452237#post1452237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone remind me, is the Air version of Dragon-Graced Weapon in non-Essence 3e a Cold attack or a wind gust for knock back?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cold.<br /> <br /> Air: Wind chills the weapon to a deadly cold. An ene-<br /> my damaged by a decisive attack takes a \u22121 penalty on <br /> physical rolls until the end of his next turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T14:42:02-07:00","id":1452239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452237#post1452237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone remind me, is the Air version of Dragon-Graced Weapon in non-Essence 3e a Cold attack or a wind gust for knock back?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Wind chills the weapon to a deadly cold. An enemy damaged by a decisive attack takes a -1 penalty on physical rolls until the end of his next turn.&quot; So, very much the same effect, though EE gets a longer duration.<br /> <br /> (Earth, on the other hand, gets knockback in 3E, straight-up damage in EE.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T15:31:25-07:00","id":1452244,"title":"","content":"Heh, well damage works well enough for my crazy Earth Aspect. Once i manage to port over his artifact over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T16:55:57-07:00","id":1452255,"title":"","content":"Flickering Shadow Evasion was a bad introduction to the charms chapter. Yuck, what a horrible charm for a simplified ruleset.<br /> <br /> But as I read more, I quite like the charms. There's fun stuff, there's straightforward stuff. There's not too many dice tricks. Some combat charms are a bit more complex than I would like, and some modes are too similar (for example, there's one where Solars ignore a flurry penalty while Sids reduce it to 1, why not have them cancel it too).<br /> Also I felt some could be a bit more clear, but hopefully editing will sort that out.<br /> <br /> I didn't love the anima banners or social system, xp and combat rules had too many mistakes that need editing, but the charms section has encouraged me back to the idea that I could run Essence rather than not run Exalted for a good few years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T01:36:10-07:00","id":1452292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452255#post1452255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flickering Shadow Evasion was a bad introduction to the charms chapter. Yuck, what a horrible charm for a simplified ruleset.<br /> <br /> But as I read more, I quite like the charms. There's fun stuff, there's straightforward stuff. There's not too many dice tricks. Some combat charms are a bit more complex than I would like, and some modes are too similar (for example, there's one where Solars ignore a flurry penalty while Sids reduce it to 1, why not have them cancel it too).<br /> Also I felt some could be a bit more clear, but hopefully editing will sort that out.<br /> <br /> I didn't love the anima banners or social system, xp and combat rules had too many mistakes that need editing, but the charms section has encouraged me back to the idea that I could run Essence rather than not run Exalted for a good few years.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are not too many dice tricks indeed, which is good. But, as mentioned in my first post, they still exist mostly in Social Charms if I'm not mistaken","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T03:51:43-07:00","id":1452300,"title":"","content":"The Getimians charms are very...very cool. Summoned from Time alone is already one of my favorite charms of all times. Looking forward to see the Sidereal charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T04:06:20-07:00","id":1452305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452300#post1452300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Getimians charms are very...very cool. Summoned from Time alone is already one of my favorite charms of all times. Looking forward to see the Sidereal charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah this is Charm is so cool !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":".  Edited because I can't read 06-15-2021, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T06:29:28-07:00","id":1452318,"title":"","content":"I'm loving all these charms, though my mind is nagging me that DBs should need more charms with Aura modes since its surprising a rarity but DBs already have the second most modes in Universals, we know that we still have the Dragon Styles to see and we have more charms on the way in the companion so I'll just have to be patient.<br /> <br /> I love how thematic all the charms are, Abyssals are just blatant and unrepentant murder while Infernals allow you to warp things horrifically alien. Alchemicals efficiency is great and Getimians ah, i personally find their charms really scary with how forceful they are. No wonder they were sealed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T07:45:05-07:00","id":1452326,"title":"","content":"Okay, new Charms! I'm going to eat my dessert first, and start with the Getimian ones.<br /> <br /> (I don't really understand what's going on with the Flowing/Stilled stuff, but that's probably a conversation for the main Essence thread, since it's a rule, not a Charm.)<br /> <br /> I wonder how many sessions it would be before I could convince another PC to drink the magical elixir I spat up with <b>Alchemic Power Reserve</b>? I was hoping that Getimians wouldn't just do weird glitch stuff, but also weird Taoist stuff.<br /> <br /> <b>Fate-Unwinding Denial</b>'s effect doesn't do it for me, but the idea of a Charm powered by banked stunts is a surprise. Not sure how I feel about it.<br /> <br /> <b>Summoned From Time</b> is a Charm with big cosmological implications - it looks like a mid-Essence Getimian can make <i>thousands</i> of people from her Origin real in Creation. To me, that says something different from &quot;these Exaltations take certain specific discarded destines and create a person around them.&quot;<br /> <br /> (I know this is likely left up to individual groups by design as well as necessity, but I really want to know how these people remember the Origin timeline - does it stop at the moment of Exaltation, or are they full of stories about things falling apart without the great hero's guidance?)<br /> <br /> <b>Devil-Queen's Court</b> is full of spooky manipulative overlord stuff, but beneath all of that, it's a cap-breaking dice adder. This concerns me.<br /> <br /> After grumping about Memetic Dogma Discipline, <b>Forgetting the Lie</b> (Flowing) gets my approval - it doesn't mess with NPCs' social rolls, but just describes what ends up happening. And what an effect it is! &quot;Why aren't you searching the compound, Cheng? The Satrap's orders were clear-&quot; &quot;No, Li, the Satrap got overthrown five years ago. What are you talking about?&quot; &quot;Oh, right, so they did. Hey, why is there some fraud using some kind of magic to make us act like the Satrap is back? We've got to warn everyone!&quot; (Li is in for a bad time if they decide to split up with Cheng, but either way, this should sow enough infighting among the guards for an easy getaway.)<br /> <br /> Also, a Charm prerequisite! So those do still exist. That's fair, so long as they're used sparingly.<br /> <br /> <b>Icon-Obliterating Passion</b> wins the award for &quot;most likely to become a mainstay in long-running internet arguments.&quot; So, the God is not the river, eh? (Cue several dozen posts debating whether the Charm itself created the God-river connection, or it already existed for the Charm to exploit.)<br /> <br /> Getimian Charms still have their theme of &quot;there are no rules to oppose this.&quot; There are LOTS of effects which appear to just happen - mostly it involves Intimacies, but definitely not all of it. Most notably, <b>Culture-Hero Usurpation</b> means that if Sha'a Oka blows one Integrity roll, the entire Silver Pact sees the Getimian as a respected luminary. They cannot resist, their memories change to accommodate this, and I don't even think the Getimian ever needs to go to The Caul or so much as see The Black Lion in person. In fairness, this one does pretty squarely fall under Destiny-Manifesting Method, but wow. <b>Throne-Smashing Ambition</b> has a similar impact - if you punch Amarel, there's nothing Fakharu can do to keep from hating her.<br /> <br /> (Oh, you don't think a Lunar elder would ever lose a rolloff with an Essence 5 Celestial? Okay, come up with the biggest mover and shaker you can imagine who has surprisingly low Integrity. Is it the head of a Great House? The sometimes-portrayed-as-totally-brainwashed Mouth of Peace? Regent Fokuf may not have any real power, but I bet that if every Dynast and Sidereal treated me as him, I could make the Realm Civil War go hot by noon tomorrow...)<br /> <br /> I hope that somebody is still using social influence in Essence, so that someday I can use (Flowing) <b>The Filial Chain</b>: you have to call the target in advance, but you can &quot;tank&quot; for less-social allies and the payoff is pure comedy. &quot;Renounce my suppression of the old religion? No, can't do that, but tell you what - I'll pay penance by having you cast off your worldly possessions and become a wandering hermit.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Flowing mode is okay, but <b>Wall-Denying Fury</b> mostly makes me happy as the first time I've thought a Still mode was way cooler. That's kind of a relief, since Autumn is the Timmy Caste I'm most likely to play. &quot;In my world, there's not a castle here, but a carnival!&quot;<br /> <br /> Oh, hey, <b>Constant Problem Tactic</b> also has a way more entertaining Still mode. Things are looking up! In an unmoving Yin kind of way. CPT is also interesting as a fairly rare case of a Charm which has a totally different role (one in combat and one outside of it) depending on the mode, which is rad.<br /> <br /> <b>One-on-One Imprisonment</b> is oddly lacking Flowing/Still modes, but remains incredibly versatile. Good for styling on a weaker enemy (to keep them from escaping), dramatic social scenes (for showing that Sidereal exactly why your world was better), and even the occasional heroic self sacrifice (alright, Mask of Winters, let's you and I step into another universe while my allies lick their wounds or run away).<br /> <br /> It seems fitting to end on <b>Unforged Masterworks</b>, since I had been meaning to close by saying that the Getimian Charms do help me to understand the old statement that they tend to skew &quot;antagonistic.&quot; A <i>lot</i> of their powers involve destroying this world's versions of things - including people - to bring in their Origin counterparts, and a magic sword of &quot;kill you forever to spend five minutes with a version of you who likes me&quot; is about the perfect summation of that.<br /> <br /> They're still at the top of my &quot;if I ever get to be a PC in this game&quot; list, but it's still worth reflecting upon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T07:57:36-07:00","id":1452329,"title":"","content":"The way I understood Getimians from what I have seen of Essence. Essentially they come from a simulation of Creation, the world they come from never existed, just a simulation. It was just a possible future/alternate history of creation. But all of them always had something that the pattern spiders/fate always was like &quot;Nope won't do that destiny&quot;. Now all these discarded destinies, aka alpha exalts projects are unsealed and manifesting in Creation with the help of the angry rogue Sidereal.<br /> <br /> Summoned From Time on another note, of course, makes me think of Fate/Stay Night popular characters like Gilgamesh or Alexander's noble phantasms abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T08:01:32-07:00","id":1452331,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, a Getimian is in Flowing or Still depending on which of their Essence pools has the larger amount currently. This is just surmise, though. It is not well-explained at all. Also, I don't know what happens if the pools are equal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T09:03:09-07:00","id":1452336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452326#post1452326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Icon-Obliterating Passion</b> wins the award for &quot;most likely to become a mainstay in long-running internet arguments.&quot; So, the God is not the river, eh? (Cue several dozen posts debating whether the Charm itself created the God-river connection, or it already existed for the Charm to exploit.)</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Begins rant.........</i>jk<br /> <br /> Though to be serious, from the wording the charm cuts the God from its connection to the Loom of Fate which seems right? God's in Exalted exist to be administrators and managers, what powers they got is usually the leeway those positions affords them. The reason they got those positions is to uphold destiny as dictated by the Loom of Fate so it all seems to make sense to me for the most part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T10:16:00-07:00","id":1452353,"title":"","content":"To be honest reading the Getimian charm preview has me a whole lot less enthused for Essence as a whole. I didn't particularly want to play one, but now I don't want to play with one or ST for one. And I'm not looking forward to being the guy in session zero asking people not to use half the &quot;new hotness&quot; cool effects. Crossing my fingers that the Sidereals don't work similar mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12165-speedbump","name":"Speedbump","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T12:27:32-07:00","id":1452365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452329#post1452329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Summoned From Time on another note, of course, makes me think of Fate/Stay Night popular characters like Gilgamesh or Alexander's noble phantasms abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, really, Summoned From Time is summoning a Servant altogether. Which really does help my F/GO Getimian idea, but does open the path to abuse. &quot;Why can't I just summon my version of Mnemon to help resolve/further fuel the civil war?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T14:05:07-07:00","id":1452372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452365#post1452365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, really, Summoned From Time is summoning a Servant altogether. Which really does help my F/GO Getimian idea, but does open the path to abuse. &quot;Why can't I just summon my version of Mnemon to help resolve/further fuel the civil war?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because Mnemon is &quot;Allies 5&quot; and you need 5 Essence <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I would also think that the Merit needs to make sense &quot;in the timeline&quot; the Getimians is coming from. If in his world, he never even met agent of The Realm, I don't think he would have access to merits related to Realm-DB like this","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T14:45:00-07:00","id":1452380,"title":"","content":"My big thought about Summoned From Time is simply that you must be Essence 3 take it. That means 3-dot Merits. Command 3 is enough for a Size 5 Battlegroup, which (at least in 3E) is 1,000 people. And &quot;the character may use an Exalt Milestone to purchase it permanently,&quot; meaning there are now 1,000 people in Creation with a memory of a world that never was.<br /> <br /> If they all really have their own pasts and memories and souls, and if you could interview each of them and find that their world is internally consistent on details that the Getimian doesn't know (and Creation doesn't share)... to me, that's a much stronger argument for discarded destinies being &quot;real&quot; worlds than the terrible fire of Exaltation bringing 64 people who never were into existence at any given time.<br /> <br /> To be clear, I like the idea that the ultimate reality or unreality of Origins is something that nobody in-universe has a definitive answer to. Even gods and sorcerers can sometimes discuss philosophy, rather than objective knowledge. But from <i>my</i> point of view, that's a compelling argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T15:20:22-07:00","id":1452382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452380#post1452380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My big thought about Summoned From Time is simply that you must be Essence 3 take it. That means 3-dot Merits. Command 3 is enough for a Size 5 Battlegroup, which (at least in 3E) is 1,000 people. And &quot;the character may use an Exalt Milestone to purchase it permanently,&quot; meaning there are now 1,000 people in Creation with a memory of a world that never was.<br /> <br /> If they all really have their own pasts and memories and souls, and if you could interview each of them and find that their world is internally consistent on details that the Getimian doesn't know (and Creation doesn't share)... to me, that's a much stronger argument for discarded destinies being &quot;real&quot; worlds than the terrible fire of Exaltation bringing 64 people who never were into existence at any given time.<br /> <br /> To be clear, I like the idea that the ultimate reality or unreality of Origins is something that nobody in-universe has a definitive answer to. Even gods and sorcerers can sometimes discuss philosophy, rather than objective knowledge. But from <i>my</i> point of view, that's a compelling argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it? You could just easily assume those beings aren't real and that the getimian just pulled people from his warped abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T18:05:01-07:00","id":1452399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452382#post1452382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it? You could just easily assume those beings aren't real and that the getimian just pulled people from his warped abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of my thought too. As far as like, the rest of reality is concerned, these guys are ss real and ahve histories as the people a Solar might make with Wyld-Shaping Technique to me. They are brought into reality, they remember something else but like....created things can be pretty internally consistent. You kind of more have a case of contagious Last Thursdayism at work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T18:55:40-07:00","id":1452406,"title":"","content":"I like the implication for Getimians who hate their original world and are trying to prevent actual Creation from becoming it. Most of their magic powers involve conjuring up stuff from their dystopian hellscape, hopefully not enough to actually cause the dystopia. It's like Kyle Reese sending back reprogrammed Terminators, or Tony Stark building a second superpowered android halfway through the movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1430-gareth3","name":"Gareth3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T19:02:16-07:00","id":1452408,"title":"","content":"I certainly see Last Thursdayism as another reasonable response, if perhaps not a very reassuring one. If a complete past is so easily counterfeited for so many, why assume that anything in Creation is older )or more &quot;real&quot;) than that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T23:02:45-07:00","id":1452418,"title":"","content":"weren't the Infernals going to have the &quot;I create a world inside me&quot; charm, or was that something for the companion? I recall someone talking about it, but I don't know if it was a promise or just someone hoping for it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T23:52:42-07:00","id":1452423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452418#post1452418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">weren't the Infernals going to have the &quot;I create a world inside me&quot; charm, or was that something for the companion? I recall someone talking about it, but I don't know if it was a promise or just someone hoping for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>there might be elements in the cards for their 3e book that the line devs haven\u2019t worked out how will work yet, and so aren\u2019t in Essence. It would not surprise me if we have \u201cand here\u2019s the Essence rules for this\u201d sidebars in some future fatsplats, or at least in their Kickstarter built Companions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T00:30:54-07:00","id":1452426,"title":"","content":"Essence is a great preview of future stuff but doubts that we will see everything. I mean Solars alone have 800+ charms in the Exalted 3rd edition core book (Even more if you include martial arts charms). Essence will not have 1000 charms for each splat but the companions bringing in new charms will show the big highlights at least. <br /> <br /> Should be noted also that the Devil Body Incarnation of Infernal is ridiculously flexible (the creation of an environment all around you can be interpreted in so many ways and making it difficult terrain for all the opponent and good for your allies).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T08:05:23-07:00","id":1452478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Speedbump</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452353#post1452353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest reading the Getimian charm preview has me a whole lot less enthused for Essence as a whole. I didn't particularly want to play one, but now I don't want to play with one or ST for one. And I'm not looking forward to being the guy in session zero asking people not to use half the &amp;quot;new hotness&amp;quot; cool effects. Crossing my fingers that the Sidereals don't work similar mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is your problem with them?<br /> <br /> I didn't like the timing on the alchemy charms. The rest seemed fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T08:06:11-07:00","id":1452479,"title":"","content":"I got unexpectedly busy yesterday (and I'm expecting more business today), but I can at least look at some more Charms right now. As they seem to be driving discussion, and also come right after Getimians, let's talk about Infernals!<br /> <br /> <b>Devil-Body Incarnation</b>, in all its glory. I really like that they put in a few less combat-focused choices: I can picture a social character going for emotion + difficult terrain (described in a way to help their social stunts, of course), or an investigative one picking X-ray vision + pass through stone. This is something every Infernal gets (though if you're not spending a Charm, maybe you should just take flight + terrain and run away), and it does read like they'd all want to.<br /> <br /> <b>Joy in Violence</b> is super odd in a world of popcorn initiative. Does this mean the whole group auto-wins Join Battle, or if the ST wins, do they automatically take back over after the player finishes?<br /> <br /> I'm beginning to think that, especially in Essence, <b>Naked Soul Insight</b> is the kind of social Charm I want to see - it has actual rules for the social influence system, if worst comes to worst, but its primary use is something else.<br /> <br /> I do not know what <b>Witness to Darkness</b>'s bonus/penalty applies to, but I really hope it's just Awareness rolls.<br /> <br /> Wait, is <b>Hideous Hundred-Limb Strike</b> implying that I can use a Step 1 reflexive Charm in response to someone else attacking me? I'm... just gonna assume this is a specific exception, and I just got too hung up on wording.<br /> <br /> <b>Acquainted with Deception</b> seems really odd in a world where Judge's Ear Technique is Universal.<br /> <br /> Laughing in your enemies' faces is apparently a physical rather than social defense, which honestly just makes it more unnerving. <b>Broken Silence Laughter Defense</b> is the first Essence Edition defensive Charm I have any real confidence in, since I'm a little uncertain over whether not getting hit is a viable plan in Essence. On the downside, I don't know whether you activate it before or after your opponent rolls damage, which is a pretty big deal, given that Infernals often want to land in one of two specific health levels.<br /> <br /> If <b>Will-Crushing Force</b> doesn't deal damage, use weapons, or interact with Soak, then why can I only use it combat and why am I spending Power equal to my target's Hardness? Why isn't this a special influence action?<br /> <br /> <b>Venom Blood Revenge</b> isn't just one of only two counterattacks in this set, it's also the first one which doesn't call for the Exalt to reflexively make a roll which is defined elsewhere as an action, and therefore (as I understand it) the only Charm we've seen so far where the &quot;counterattacks count as actions&quot; rule means anything. It is also the only source so far to explicitly deal <i>dice</i> of environmental damage, which is notable, because it's usually not stated what environmental damage is, exactly - the systems chapter has an example which implies levels, whilst Elemental Bolt Attack is totally insane unless it's dice.<br /> <br /> Everything 3E taught me about Soak Charms has been upended by <b>Viridian Rust Defense</b>. What, Charms will help my durability most when I'm already wearing armor? Unthinkable!<br /> <br /> <b>Dark Miracle Mimicry</b> is a cool concept, but also the first of the Infernal Charms that I'm actually uncertain how I would run in play. Its requirements are all about the target, not the ability copied, so I do not know whether the intent is that the Infernal needs to have seen it used. That's a big difference, not least because it might allow this Charm to &quot;scan&quot; enemy powers (it already implicitly does that for Essence rating, but I don't know whether that's ever hidden information). At the far opposite end of utility, it also never says the player picks the power, so they might get something random.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Spite Curse</b> does seem to outright confirm that, outside of attacks, you can use reflexive Step 1 Charms on Step 1 of someone else's actions. This concerns me.<br /> <br /> That's a bitter note to end on, when overall, I thought these Charms looked really good! I like how many classic &quot;boss fight&quot; abilities they worked into the combat Charms - heck, I liked that they had a suite of combat Charms. I'm not sure whether Getimians are supposed to be bad at fighting (given their Ox-Body), or just very reliant upon martial arts, but they did not get many of those. Getimian stuff fired my imagination more, but Infernal Charms are the ones were I could play with a stranger who read the same book and feel like we'd be on the same page more than half of the time. It does seem surprising (not bad, but unexpected) that Infernal social Charms are heavily geared towards either gathering information or messing with the mind of one specific person - they don't seem to have any native way to change minds on a larger scale, with the closest thing being Unbreakable Laws of Hell (which can only change actions). If that's deliberate, it plays an interesting part in the question of Infernals' ability to make real positive reforms rather than just bringing calamity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T08:07:04-07:00","id":1452480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452318#post1452318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm loving all these charms, though my mind is nagging me that DBs should need more charms with Aura modes since its surprising a rarity but DBs already have the second most modes in Universals, we know that we still have the Dragon Styles to see and we have more charms on the way in the companion so I'll just have to be patient.<br /> <br /> I love how thematic all the charms are, Abyssals are just blatant and unrepentant murder while Infernals allow you to warp things horrifically alien. Alchemicals efficiency is great and Getimians ah, i personally find their charms really scary with how forceful they are. No wonder they were sealed.</div> </div> </div> </div>As it is supposed to be a simpler system, I was surprised they left in Aura at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T08:23:09-07:00","id":1452483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452480#post1452480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As it is supposed to be a simpler system, I was surprised they left in Aura at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>True though to be honest compared to 3e, for Aura they have is way way simpler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T08:49:09-07:00","id":1452485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452479#post1452479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Joy in Violence</b> is super odd in a world of popcorn initiative. Does this mean the whole group auto-wins Join Battle, or if the ST wins, do they automatically take back over after the player finishes?<br /> <br /> I'm beginning to think that, especially in Essence, <b>Naked Soul Insight</b> is the kind of social Charm I want to see - it has actual rules for the social influence system, if worst comes to worst, but its primary use is something else.<br /> <br /> I do not know what <b>Witness to Darkness</b>'s bonus/penalty applies to, but I really hope it's just Awareness rolls.<br /> <br /> Wait, is <b>Hideous Hundred-Limb Strike</b> implying that I can use a Step 1 reflexive Charm in response to someone else attacking me? I'm... just gonna assume this is a specific exception, and I just got too hung up on wording.<br /> <br /> <b>Acquainted with Deception</b> seems really odd in a world where Judge's Ear Technique is Universal.<br /> <br /> Laughing in your enemies' faces is apparently a physical rather than social defense, which honestly just makes it more unnerving. <b>Broken Silence Laughter Defense</b> is the first Essence Edition defensive Charm I have any real confidence in, since I'm a little uncertain over whether not getting hit is a viable plan in Essence. On the downside, I don't know whether you activate it before or after your opponent rolls damage, which is a pretty big deal, given that Infernals often want to land in one of two specific health levels.<br /> <br /> If <b>Will-Crushing Force</b> doesn't deal damage, use weapons, or interact with Soak, then why can I only use it combat and why am I spending Power equal to my target's Hardness? Why isn't this a special influence action?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had the same thought reading those charms. The &quot;Step 1&quot; reflexive Charm on someone else turns does seem very strange, but I don't see how this might work on any other way ? Maybe they should clarify something like &quot;This is one unique case where one can use his Charms on Step 1 from someone else&quot; but I don't know if that's true or not","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T09:06:15-07:00","id":1452486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452485#post1452485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had the same thought reading those charms. The &quot;Step 1&quot; reflexive Charm on someone else turns does seem very strange, but I don't see how this might work on any other way ? Maybe they should clarify something like &quot;This is one unique case where one can use his Charms on Step 1 from someone else&quot; but I don't know if that's true or not</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my first impulse, but then Shadow Spite Curse talked about the same thing.<br /> <br /> So... does Perfected Shining Summons let me create armor in response to being attacked? Can I turn on Eagle-Wing Style when someone pulls the lever to drop the floor out from under me? I'm obviously not supposed to use Many-Attacks Technique on my opponent's step one to get a pseudo-counterattack after theirs resolves... right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T09:17:58-07:00","id":1452489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452483#post1452483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True though to be honest compared to 3e, for Aura they have is way way simpler.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is much simpler, yes. But still feels a bit unnecessary.<br /> <br /> Actually a lot of ExEss feels like that to me: some things have been simplified, but there's a lot that haven't, and could easily be. So it ends up with quicker combat, and outside that, it's about 20% simpler. Still a lot more complex than a lot of RPGs though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T09:21:58-07:00","id":1452490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452479#post1452479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, is <b>Hideous Hundred-Limb Strike</b> implying that I can use a Step 1 reflexive Charm in response to someone else attacking me? I'm... just gonna assume this is a specific exception, and I just got too hung up on wording.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's step 1 of your attack, and thus you can't use any other Step 1 Charm on that attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Laughing in your enemies' faces is apparently a physical rather than social defense, which honestly just makes it more unnerving. <b>Broken Silence Laughter Defense</b> is the first Essence Edition defensive Charm I have any real confidence in, since I'm a little uncertain over whether not getting hit is a viable plan in Essence. On the downside, I don't know whether you activate it before or after your opponent rolls damage, which is a pretty big deal, given that Infernals often want to land in one of two specific health levels. </div> </div> </div>I think after, but this might be one for the errata form. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If <b>Will-Crushing Force</b> doesn't deal damage, use weapons, or interact with Soak, then why can I only use it combat and why am I spending Power equal to my target's Hardness? Why isn't this a special influence action? </div> </div> </div>Seems like its flavor description is violent and threatening enough that it wouldn't make sense to use outside of combat situations...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Venom Blood Revenge</b> isn't just one of only two counterattacks in this set, it's also the first one which doesn't call for the Exalt to reflexively make a roll which is defined elsewhere as an action, and therefore (as I understand it) the only Charm we've seen so far where the &quot;counterattacks count as actions&quot; rule means anything. </div> </div> </div>I think Build Power rolls aren't the same as Build Power actions...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is also the only source so far to explicitly deal <i>dice</i> of environmental damage, which is notable, because it's usually not stated what environmental damage is, exactly - the systems chapter has an example which implies levels, whilst Elemental Bolt Attack is totally insane unless it's dice. </div> </div> </div>I would put that in the errata form somewhere...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Dark Miracle Mimicry</b> is a cool concept, but also the first of the Infernal Charms that I'm actually uncertain how I would run in play. Its requirements are all about the target, not the ability copied, so I do not know whether the intent is that the Infernal needs to have seen it used. That's a big difference, not least because it might allow this Charm to &quot;scan&quot; enemy powers (it already implicitly does that for Essence rating, but I don't know whether that's ever hidden information). At the far opposite end of utility, it also never says the player picks the power, so they might get something random. </div> </div> </div>I would interpret it as you get to pick and you have to know what it is, by seeing it or by another method, you can't scan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Shadow Spite Curse</b> does seem to outright confirm that, outside of attacks, you can use reflexive Step 1 Charms on Step 1 of someone else's actions. This concerns me. </div> </div> </div>Why does that concern you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T09:43:31-07:00","id":1452493,"title":"","content":"God only knows why the Alchemical Charm switch is here and not in the rules for the Rite of Reconfiguration, and why it's not an Exalt Advantage (though they're hardly the only splat that has to pretend they don't have a fourth Advantage). It's better than nothing, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T10:07:48-07:00","id":1452497,"title":"","content":"My bigger worry is Poor Abyssals and Infernals, with the bonus <i>disadvantage</i> of being Creatures of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452490#post1452490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think after, but this might be one for the errata form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm making liberal use of the errata form. Sometimes right away, sometimes after discussing things with others, in public or private, to see if anyone else is confused (or worse, totally confident, but of different readings) by the same things I am.<br /> <br /> This is a perfect example of how vague wording leads to good faith misunderstandings, by the way, after I had been doubting myself thinking maybe Broken Silence Laughter Defense didn't need errata, because Wrath-Stoked Onslaught seemed to imply that Step 6 Charms are used before a damage roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think Build Power rolls aren't the same as Build Power actions... </div> </div> </div>This is also what I initially thought. It's totally unclear in the text.<br /> <br /> My current view is because a writer apparently said on the Discord that the Build Power from Spectral Deception counts as one of your actions. &quot;If [a Charm] creates an action, it will specify,&quot; says the Using Charms section, and that Charm doesn't, so I tried to reason out a general rule which the text might be implying but not outright stating. &quot;Anything the general rules defines as an action is always an action, unless specified&quot; was my best guess. In the cases I've noticed, that seems to clear things up and maintain balance - I'd like to hear of cases where other people see it applying, for good or ill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would interpret it as you get to pick and you have to know what it is, by seeing it or by another method, you can't scan. </div> </div> </div>That's a reasonable interpretation, and the sort of thing it's well worth sharing with a player who is considering taking this Charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it's step 1 of your attack, and thus you can't use any other Step 1 Charm on that attack. </div> </div> </div>It is. But it can somehow also create a clash, and you don't have a Step 1 of your own action at that point, which implies that you must be firing it on Step 1 of someone else's action. That's not needed for the clash to function, because creating a clash on Step 2 explicitly sends both combatants back to Step 1, so it feels worryingly like an insight into the writers not having actually meant what I thought they did with their timing rules.<br /> <br /> As for why that other version of timing concerns me, well, to pull a few random examples out of the aether...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452486#post1452486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... does Perfected Shining Summons let me create armor in response to being attacked? Can I turn on Eagle-Wing Style when someone pulls the lever to drop the floor out from under me? I'm obviously not supposed to use Many-Attacks Technique on my opponent's step one to get a pseudo-counterattack after theirs resolves... right?</div> </div> </div> </div>More broadly, it seems to me that the intention of &quot;if a Charm has no listed Step, treat it as a Step 1&quot; is that it limits the amount of stuff you can do at any one time. You can use those Charms on your own actions - usually that means your turn, and it almost always means only twice per round (plus the opportunity costs of not using Charms which specifically help the action you're taking, if any). But if everyone's Step 1s are in play, then even a moderate-sized fight probably lets you fire off all the Reflexive Charms you want to (and can afford) on any given round. That would be a huge re-assessment of large swaths of the game, so not knowing which one the writers had in mind when they designed and tested it is concerning.<br /> <br /> Here's an example goofier than anything I listed above: in a fight with 10+ combatants, is it really desirable for an Essence 3 Solar to be able to commit a mote to Perfected Shining Summons each turn, hit Bonfire in round 1, then drop all the commitments to be at full motes? (And maybe also their whole circle is at Power 10 - see also Build Power rolls versus Build Power actions.)<br /> <br /> I would argue it is not. I will read these Charms as explicit exceptions to normal timing rules until the writers say otherwise. But I do prefer it when rulebooks don't make me guess on stuff like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":2168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","user":"Chejop Kejak","date":". 06-16-2021, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T11:50:39-07:00","id":1452512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452489#post1452489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is much simpler, yes. But still feels a bit unnecessary.<br /> <br /> Actually a lot of ExEss feels like that to me: some things have been simplified, but there's a lot that haven't, and could easily be. So it ends up with quicker combat, and outside that, it's about 20% simpler. Still a lot more complex than a lot of RPGs though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much the point. The main goal of Essence was to allow it to be more easy to play for newcomers while also not totally getting rid a lot of the systems and mechanics that people like of 3e. From the devs words, ExEss is as complicated as a non-mage CofD splat, plenty of mechanics to interact with but with some work to make it intuitive","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T13:24:47-07:00","id":1452526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452512#post1452512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's pretty much the point. The main goal of Essence was to allow it to be more easy to play for newcomers while also not totally getting rid a lot of the systems and mechanics that people like of 3e. From the devs words, ExEss is as complicated as a non-mage CofD splat, plenty of mechanics to interact with but with some work to make it intuitive</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are there two charms for making battlegroups better?<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, in general Essence is fine. But there's a lot of Charms that are really whack. You can speak extra languages with an Embassy roll. Or you can buy an Embassy Charm to speak extra languages... but when you get too powerful you take a massive penalty when you speak those languages.<br /> <br /> Essence could be a LOT more streamlined.<br /> <br /> How many types of milestone are there?<br /> <br /> Charm modes that list Solar and Abyssal... and then separately lists another mode that says &quot;works the same as the solar mode&quot;?<br /> <br /> Multiple different system terms that refer to the same thing?<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, massive love to the Essence team, and full acknowledgement that this is still beta... but this could be a LOT simpler and maintain the same level of verisimilitude. And I'm pretty sure, say, Vampire, is still simpler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T14:35:18-07:00","id":1452536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452526#post1452526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why are there two charms for making battlegroups better?<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, in general Essence is fine. But there's a lot of Charms that are really whack. You can speak extra languages with an Embassy roll. Or you can buy an Embassy Charm to speak extra languages... but when you get too powerful you take a massive penalty when you speak those languages.<br /> <br /> Essence could be a LOT more streamlined.<br /> <br /> How many types of milestone are there?<br /> <br /> Charm modes that list Solar and Abyssal... and then separately lists another mode that says &amp;quot;works the same as the solar mode&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> Multiple different system terms that refer to the same thing?<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, massive love to the Essence team, and full acknowledgement that this is still beta... but this could be a LOT simpler and maintain the same level of verisimilitude. And I'm pretty sure, say, Vampire, is still simpler.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the feeling some of them are legit mistakes and other are their perspective on the game (like say the milestones maybe). <br /> <br /> Whats a bit frustrating is I feel they dont share their insight on design choices that much and the few times I've seen question asked on their design choices there was no discussion possible. Maybe its because there are inner circle of people with answers of these questions, but as someone who only participate in the kickstarter I feel its pretty opaque.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T14:55:08-07:00","id":1452543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452536#post1452536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whats a bit frustrating is I feel they dont share their insight on design choices that much and the few times I've seen question asked on their design choices there was no discussion possible. Maybe its because there are inner circle of people with answers of these questions, but as someone who only participate in the kickstarter I feel its pretty opaque.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have some similar concerns, but it's worth noting that I have seen some discussion of the writers publicly posting the process of, say, putting together a new Antagonist. If several of those happen, it would be really cool and useful as a stronger insight into how the writers are using this system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T23:23:43-07:00","id":1452583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452512#post1452512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's pretty much the point. The main goal of Essence was to allow it to be more easy to play for newcomers while also not totally getting rid a lot of the systems and mechanics that people like of 3e. From the devs words, ExEss is as complicated as a non-mage CofD splat, plenty of mechanics to interact with but with some work to make it intuitive</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally feel pretty strongly that having Steps but not action types on Charms just makes stuff straight-up worse for newcomers than most of the CofD games, for the basic resolution issues that have already been mentioned in this thread. Heck, even just doing it exactly the opposite way (clearly defined action types and rules using those for actions-per-turn, while leaving the steps of combat resolution implicit) would be much closer to how basically every bigger-name RPG on the market operates, and it would still play basically the same way as long as there were clear rules on triggered effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T02:38:01-07:00","id":1452598,"title":"","content":"I definitely think Essence is more complex than Vampire or Werewolf, no doubt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T02:46:16-07:00","id":1452599,"title":"","content":"I think it's also more complicated than the last editions of Mage, which ran rather smoothly when I played it (ok except for the sort of Anima stuff they included in Mage). There are some subsystems, but they work in a simple way. here I have a feeling there are too much exceptions everywhere, which makes things hard to track and remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T06:32:51-07:00","id":1452616,"title":"","content":"My experience running Mage is it's sort of simple, but in a complex way. The basic rules aren't that complicated, but how they work in practice is effectively quite complicated. A lot of adjudication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T06:42:42-07:00","id":1452617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452616#post1452616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My experience running Mage is it's sort of simple, but in a complex way. The basic rules aren't that complicated, but how they work in practice is effectively quite complicated. A lot of adjudication.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. <br /> <br /> On another topic, I still can't say if Excellencies allow you to augment your Resolve, and the Destiny-Manifesting Charm for Solars is starting to make me thing that you can't","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T06:44:11-07:00","id":1452619,"title":"","content":"Can't you use excellencies to boost static values outside combat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T06:49:04-07:00","id":1452620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452619#post1452619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't you use excellencies to boost static values outside combat?</div> </div> </div> </div>yes, but Resolve is not a static value calculated directly as Integrity+Attribute/2 or anything like that, it's a base value set depending on a threshold from Integrity, which makes me doubt, and most people I've talked with about that were not convinced either 100% that you could actually boost it with Excellencies","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T06:59:34-07:00","id":1452621,"title":"","content":"I think that you can boost Resolve, but Chausse is making an interesting point. Excellencies say this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Essence Edition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When purchasing this Charm, choose an Ability. Spend 1 mote. This applies on Step 1 during combat. Outside of combat, this may be used to boost passive values. Add that Ability as a dice bonus to an applicable roll involving the chosen Ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elsewhere in the book, they explain that adding dice to a passive value means that you add dice/2, rounded up. But neither the section on bonuses nor the Excellency Charm itself tells us <i>which</i> passive values we can use the Excellency on. It doesn't mention any restrictions at all! Technically, I could argue that Invincible Sword Princess is allowed to use her flawless dedication to the sword in order to boost her Resolve or Soak... but only outside of combat.<br /> <br /> That's obviously not the intention. But what is? Outside of combat, using Defense is pretty rare, and as for the other static values...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Essence Edition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without armor, your Soak is 1, plus another 1 if your Fortitude is higher than 3. If you are wearing armor, add the Armor Soak Value to this total.<br /> <br /> Characters start with a Hardness 2 plus any applicable bonuses from armor. Exalted characters add their Essence rating to their Hardness value.<br /> <br /> Characters have a Resolve against social influence set to two modified by the character\u2019s Intimacy, Virtue, and Integrity. If the character has at least one dot in the Integrity Ability, her Resolve is set to three, and if the Integrity Ability is three or higher, her Resolve is four instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of those, even Resolve, is a calculation involving Ability/2. But if Resolve is not the static value we're expected to boost outside of combat, what is that sentence in the Excellency even talking about? It's a little puzzling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T08:01:54-07:00","id":1452630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452621#post1452621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that you can boost Resolve, but Chausse is making an interesting point. Excellencies say this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Elsewhere in the book, they explain that adding dice to a passive value means that you add dice/2, rounded up. But neither the section on bonuses nor the Excellency Charm itself tells us <i>which</i> passive values we can use the Excellency on. It doesn't mention any restrictions at all! Technically, I could argue that Invincible Sword Princess is allowed to use her flawless dedication to the sword in order to boost her Resolve or Soak... but only outside of combat.<br /> <br /> That's obviously not the intention. But what is? Outside of combat, using Defense is pretty rare, and as for the other static values...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> None of those, even Resolve, is a calculation involving Ability/2. But if Resolve is not the static value we're expected to boost outside of combat, what is that sentence in the Excellency even talking about? It's a little puzzling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah good point, there are basically no other static values outside of Defense out of combat, so I guess Resolve but be boostable with the Integrity Excellency. This makes Destiny-Manifesting Method a bit weird (a low-Integrity Charm that boost as much as a high ability Excellency), but I guess it's not strictly incompatible","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T08:15:46-07:00","id":1452633,"title":"","content":"It says &quot;passive values,&quot; and Resolve is a passive value no matter how it's calculated. So, if you have an excellency which would be applicable to raising your Resolve, then you should be able to do it out of combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T08:51:25-07:00","id":1452638,"title":"","content":"So Wyld-Shaping Technique in Essence. Does it still allow land creation or is it stuck to items. I'm hoping that I just misread it and that they didn't loose their ability to go into the Wyld and make land and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T09:24:23-07:00","id":1452643,"title":"","content":"Still just skimming through the charms released today, but is it just me, or does &quot;Orichalcum Battle Soul&quot; feel a bit . . . redundant with the solar mode of &quot;Fists of Iron&quot;? Like, Fist of iron does a bit more and its activation is less narrow, but I'd imagine that you'll be able to justify fighting for a virtue or intimacy fairly often, and anyone who wants fists of iron probably wants the extra things that OBS does, too. We'll have to see how impactful weapon tags are (and how big the distinction between the weapon weights are), but my gut reaction is just that the overlap there feels a bit bad. I've talked myself into thinking it's probably not a huge thing, though . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5849-whiskey-jack","name":"Whiskey Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T09:28:12-07:00","id":1452645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452633#post1452633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says &quot;passive values,&quot; and Resolve is a passive value no matter how it's calculated. So, if you have an excellency which would be applicable to raising your Resolve, then you should be able to do it out of combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... can I use my unfaltering dedication to the blade (Close Combat Excellency) to raise my Resolve?<br /> <br /> What about my understanding of different people and cultures (Embassy Excellency)?<br /> <br /> Can I bump my Soak and Hardness with an Excellency?<br /> <br /> If someone makes a social roll against me <i>as their combat action</i> can I use my Integrity Excellency to boost my Resolve? And, if not, what stops my players starting combat every time they want to negotiate?<br /> <br /> &quot;And now, we discuss terms of the trade agreement. Draw your sword.&quot;<br /> <br /> I say put in an errata form and get the wording cleared up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452638#post1452638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Wyld-Shaping Technique in Essence. Does it still allow land creation or is it stuck to items. I'm hoping that I just misread it and that they didn't loose their ability to go into the Wyld and make land and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it does make land. Might be good for a feedback form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-17-2021, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T09:59:00-07:00","id":1452649,"title":"","content":"I had really thought that the relative lull in my life would extend through the whole Essence manuscript, but it was not to be. I've only been managing one really attentive read of a Charmset per day, and right now, I've only skimmed Abyssals (they seemed cool and flavorful) and Dragon-Blooded (I had no specific complaints, but I felt like something was missing - I hope to figure that out when I really break everything down). I haven't read Alchemical Charms at all.<br /> <br /> That's on the to-do list, but today another manuscript dropped, and this one contains my favorite splat in the game! Besides, I've been skipping around the whole time anyway. Surely, nobody will blame for diving into Lunars!<br /> <br /> (What? You thought something else was my favorite? But whatever for?)<br /> <br /> Right off the bat, I'm reminded that there's a lot of things here I won't understand until I've seen the animal rules. That's fairly usual for shapeshifting, of course, and I am heartened that &quot;a list of one-off special traits&quot; is the sort of thing which people can curate and balance, unlike the 3E &quot;full statblocks loaded with special exceptions&quot; version, which... well, that'd be a whole other thread.<br /> <br /> <b>Changing Phases Transformation</b> is the answer to people who wanted the omni-Excellent Lunar. It's not a perfect answer (certainly no 7-die Excellency to every possible pool) but it is the only way to start with a 5-dot Attribute in by-the-book EE, and if you have any advance warning about what you're doing, it can always be the right Attribute. Does your stooped old witch need to topple a statue? Force 5 will do for this scene. Got exposed to a supernatural plague? Time for Fortitude 5 until you fight it off. Versatile.<br /> <br /> Once again, I am pretty dubious of <b>Deadly Beastman Transformation</b>. Infernals can get a scenelong +2 Soak without reducing their Defense, why take a penalty for a mere +1? On the other hand, <b>Hybrid Body Transformation</b> looks like a crucial combat buff. +2 successes to many of your attacks (and certainly Decisive ones) should be doable with most combat-oriented shapes. I don't know how to read the implication that this could instead boost Defense, however, since it also uses the word &quot;actions&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's kind of funny that I never considered using <b>Mountainous Spirit Expression</b> on a human form until the book told me I had to wait until Essence 3 and buy it again. Honestly, though, forget your <i>true</i> human shape - the real style points are for stealing the face of the Satrap's secret lover, childhood best friend, or sternest old school teacher, then lecturing the whole city on their evil deeds in the form of a kaiju-sized ghost from their past. Keep things surreal.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, no love for Tyrant Mouse Dominion. I suppose that a Charm must be good for more than <i>just</i> keeping things surreal.<br /> <br /> <b>Hungry All-Consuming Cloud</b> seems odd. It's the only Finesse 5 Charm Lunars get, but has an effect scaled off of Fortitude. It has 3E-style verbiage that &quot;only the highest withering damage roll made grants Power,&quot; which doesn't seem needed with EE's withering rules. I don't really know what the last sentence means. I am reporting this one as a probable version error.<br /> <br /> Wow, <b>Laughing Devil Distraction</b> is a brutal debuff. One more piece of evidence on the pile of &quot;Defense looks terrible in Essence.&quot;<br /> <br /> Oddly, <b>Quicksilver Second Face</b> lets you freely take a form you've already assumed this scene, when the 3E version of that build (via Ever-Evolving Defense) winds up trying to pick a new form each action.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Talon Execution</b> lets a character making an attack from stealth gain a bonus to their next War Project action! Ah, versioning errors.<br /> <br /> Hey, <b>Beast-Soul Awakening</b> is a Charm which seems like it should make a special Project, and actually does just that! Nice.<br /> <br /> It had not occurred to me that a character could not freely participate in social influence outside of combat time while holding someone in a headlock, until <b>Grasping Pseudopod Method</b> said it could let me sidestep that problem. Sure, in real life, wrestling of any kind tends to leave a body short on both breath and attention, but in action-adventure world, this surprised me - another of my failures to read the authors' default assumptions.<br /> <br /> <b>Insidious Lunar Transformation</b> has nothing to say about the target's traits while transformed. Surely they're not meant to keep all their best pools, like a Lunar does, but I don't know what really happens. I'm waiting to see Antagonists, but feel like something is missing.<br /> <br /> Does <b>Adder Fang Method </b>let me poison someone with a Withering attack? If so, does that attack &quot;hit&quot; when it rolled below their Defense, but still got me Overwhelm-based Power?<br /> <br /> <b>Creation-Spanning Passion</b> (a Charm which I instantly like better now that it acts on existing relationships and drops the bonus to rolls to establish them) mentions Solar Mates. I do a quick search, and see it is the only one to do so. However, I seem to have not registered a few things in earlier manuscripts: the Lunar mode for Integrity-Protecting Principle did this, and the term is used twice (though never explained) in the Storytelling chapter. I really wonder what someone new to Exalted would make of this, especially a non-ST who first sees those words jump out of nowhere mid-Charm.<br /> <br /> Upon reaching <b>Relentless Lunar Fury</b>, I realize that there have been relatively few combat-oriented Charms, and they've all leaned into very narrow fighting styles and/or aesthetics: the &quot;beastman&quot; Universal Charms, the &quot;duplicates&quot; stuff in Finesse, the grappling ones in Force, and Adder-Fang Method. This is the <i>only</i> native Lunar Charm to seem generally applicable to a wide range of combat characters.<br /> <br /> The rules are kind of odd, though. It gets activated on Step 7, but doesn't specify it has to be Step 7 of a decisive attack against the Lunar, so you can apparently go berserk on your own first Withering attack. Maybe they just don't want a Lunar to use the pseudo-Knife Biting Attitude the same turn that she puts RLF up, but again, that just encourages people to pop it early in any fight where they might need it. Also, you really want to exceed 10 Power, since unlike the Greater Sign of Mars, going above 10 Power lets you bank bonus damage <i>successes</i>. Eeep.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I want <b>Shattered Yoke Fury</b> to be the general rule, instead of just letting you shrug off anything that doesn't fit your vision of the character. &quot;Form an Intimacy and take an immediate dramatic action&quot; is a much more gameable concept than &quot;give them a small number of bonus dice.&quot;<br /> <br /> Overall, I think these Charms look fun, and did a good job of selling what Lunars are to new players. People should come away from this list with the idea that Lunars are tricky folklore-ish figures. The combat Charms tend to be oddly narrow (no self-healing?), and there are definitely favorite tricks I'm sad not to see (priority one is bringing back the Many-Pockets Meditation tree, after that I can try more complicated stuff like Mirror Slip Trick), but there's not a lot here which I don't think justifies its presence. The only hole that really makes me scratch my head is how limited their social suite is - Predator-and-Prey Mirror seems to literally be the only way to influence others' intimacies in the whole set. I think that someone with no context beyond this book would see Lunars as loners who bless groups they like and steal shapes from those they dislike, but don't try to sway what those people do beyond being strong or being dead.<br /> <br /> Writing it out, that's not all wrong, but it is pretty extreme. As with Infernals getting lots of tricks to mess with one person but very little to convince the crowd, I'm not sure how much of this is space limitations and how much is a deliberate statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":2168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","user":"Chejop Kejak","date":". 06-17-2021, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T10:23:59-07:00","id":1452653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452645#post1452645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... can I use my unfaltering dedication to the blade (Close Combat Excellency) to raise my Resolve?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it applicable to the situation and involve the ability? Since Resolve is calculated using Integrity, Close Combat shouldn't be usable. However, if you have an intimacy relating to your blade, it would increase your Resolve when applicable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about my understanding of different people and cultures (Embassy Excellency)? </div> </div> </div>Again, Resolve isn't calculated from Embassy. Not applicable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can I bump my Soak and Hardness with an Excellency? </div> </div> </div>Not in combat, but if you had a Fortitude Excellency, you could increase your Soak outside of combat. Hardness isn't based off of an ability or attribute. Excellencies wouldn't apply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If someone makes a social roll against me <i>as their combat action</i> can I use my Integrity Excellency to boost my Resolve? </div> </div> </div>Not RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, if not, what stops my players starting combat every time they want to negotiate? </div> </div> </div>First, it usually won't benefit them since Excellencies are rarer than in 3e. Second, they'll have a decent chance of triggering Virtues and Intimacies by putting people's lives on the line, which could increase the difficulty instead of making it easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T10:43:08-07:00","id":1452654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452649#post1452649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall, I think these Charms look fun, and did a good job of selling what Lunars are to new players. People should come away from this list with the idea that Lunars are tricky folklore-ish figures. The combat Charms tend to be oddly narrow (no self-healing?),</div> </div> </div> </div>Biggest miss imo for Essence Lunars is them missing Regen charm which has been part of them and talked a lot .... <br /> Not even one at all.... And it saddens me that they totally butchered Lunar Regen characters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T12:06:37-07:00","id":1452666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whiskey Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452643#post1452643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still just skimming through the charms released today, but is it just me, or does &quot;Orichalcum Battle Soul&quot; feel a bit . . . redundant with the solar mode of &quot;Fists of Iron&quot;? Like, Fist of iron does a bit more and its activation is less narrow, but I'd imagine that you'll be able to justify fighting for a virtue or intimacy fairly often, and anyone who wants fists of iron probably wants the extra things that OBS does, too. We'll have to see how impactful weapon tags are (and how big the distinction between the weapon weights are), but my gut reaction is just that the overlap there feels a bit bad. I've talked myself into thinking it's probably not a huge thing, though . . .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree it is a bit redundant yeah but from the looks of it OBS allows you to pick up artifact armor without actually needing armor so if your concept is a bare-chested brawler of invincible might its probably for that but yeah<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T12:25:54-07:00","id":1452670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452621#post1452621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of those, even Resolve, is a calculation involving Ability/2. But if Resolve is not the static value we're expected to boost outside of combat, what is that sentence in the Excellency even talking about? It's a little puzzling.</div> </div> </div> </div>This argument, in my opinion, settles the issue: The text does not say static values need to be calculated using Ability/2 to be boosted by the Excellency, and no static values are calculated using Ability/2 anyways, so that's not what it means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T12:54:19-07:00","id":1452677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452654#post1452654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Biggest miss imo for Essence Lunars is them missing Regen charm which has been part of them and talked a lot ....<br /> Not even one at all.... And it saddens me that they totally butchered Lunar Regen characters</div> </div> </div> </div>The saving grace on this one is that Essence's greater degree of cross-splat balance makes something like just stealing Reinforced Chassis/Body Reweaving Matrix into a more reasonable-seeming option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452670#post1452670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This argument, in my opinion, settles the issue: The text does not say static values need to be calculated using Ability/2 to be boosted by the Excellency, and no static values are calculated using Ability/2 anyways, so that's not what it means.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to agree (as I said in the post you yourself are quoting, I think it's clear that the intent is Integrity Excellency helping with Resolve), but it is worth noting that the text doesn't establish <i>any</i> requirements for boosting a static value with an Excellency. As written, JohnDoe is correct that any Excellency can boost any static value.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T13:10:38-07:00","id":1452681,"title":"","content":"My above ribbing aside, I am going to (time permitting) cover the Charms of my old favorite (and, alas, still-namesake) splat.<br /> <br /> <b>Absence</b> looks good, though I am sad that a new wave of Sidereal players will try to get out of conversations by shouting that, rather the more-cumbersome but more amusing &quot;Avoidance Kata!&quot; - hey, if there's any splat where I can be a grumpy old geezer, it's this one. It also seems like an odd choice that (1) the Sidereal knows if everyone forgets them, and (2) more people forgetting you makes it harder to hide. Huh.<br /> <br /> <b>Invisible Motion</b> fills me with questions. I don't know if it's an old version, or if I was meant to deduce a ton of limitations on Inexorable Advance back in universal modes. At first blush, the Essence 1 Charm seems to do a lot more, but now I presume that you only get the &quot;flash step&quot; effect only happens on a rush, rather than all movement actions? I have no idea whether any of the other Sid/Get Charms which make movement into a short-range teleport are meant to go through walls.<br /> <br /> The pet Pattern Spider from <b>Efficient Secretary Technique</b> can no longer tell you who stabbed Sesus Lahor. I <i>can</i> provide a bonus to any non &quot;combat-related&quot; action, which is neat, but make me wonder whether planning a military campaign counts. Also, can it help me when my action is teamwork for an ally? Hopefully not, due to Pattern Spiders infamously hating recursion.<br /> <br /> I think <b>Last Vision</b> is new, and I secretly hope it was created explicitly so that we can all solve the murder of Sesus Lahor, now that the spiders won't tell. It does, otherwise, feel like a very odd choice for a Sidereal Charm.<br /> <br /> This is mostly errata stuff, but if you spend stunt dice on <b>Of Truths Best Unknown</b>, you technically gain 2 Anima, due to that Charm duplicating the general note at the start of Sidereal Charms. This is actually kind of a tricky problem, since mechanical notes in the lore sentence at the start of any given Charm section are easy to overlook.<br /> <br /> Okay, <b>Mending Warped Designs</b>, but <i>why</i> am I rolling Finesse + Craft? What's the difficulty, what happens if I succeed or fail? The implication seems to be &quot;Difficulty 3&quot; (because none is specified) and &quot;the Charm fails&quot; (because this only comes up when opposing powerful effects), but I'm purely speculating here.<br /> <br /> <b>Cash and Murder Games</b> keeps the awesome name while getting rid of the creepiest language and effects. That makes me very happy, so I feel a little bad that I'm now wondering if this now requires the Sidereal to be in the same place as both targets at once, and if not, what that means for any other Charms which create new influence actions if they don't give details on range - and Essence almost never does.<br /> <br /> Impossible-to-resist effects aren't just for Getimians, since a Sidereal can <b>End Debate</b>.<br /> <br /> There's been a lot of discussion about Hard Bargains versus opting out of social influence lately, so it's interesting to me that <b>Icy Hand</b> gives you further benefits if people take the former but <i>not</i> the latter. An odd inversion of Fate-Unwinding Denial and Devil Emperor Edict.<br /> <br /> I'm not the biggest fan of things which get extremely literal with the &quot;Divine Bureaucracy&quot; thing, but <b>Secret Sinecure Agreement</b> has some very cool roleplaying possibilities.<br /> <br /> With <b>Indecision is Death</b>, I officially have no idea how the writers are expecting me to use the influence system.<br /> <br /> <b>Sculpting the Wild Lands</b> is the <i>best</i> special project-making Charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Abandoned Words Curse</b> finally makes it official: being incapable of speech is a four-die penalty to influence. I am now convinced that the penalty for Language-Learning Ritual is meant to be dice, since otherwise, using a Charm to magically learn a language is no better for communication than just using pantomime.<br /> <br /> Charms which don't count as Charms is not my favorite design space, but than again, if <b>Defense of Shining Joy</b> <i>did</i> count as using a Charm, I have no idea when it would happen, so I assume that was their thinking as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Faultless Ceremony</b> sure thinks we're going to keep a lot of stunt dice in the pool. But the 2:1 ratio has me confused - when Sidereal Charms talk about spending stunt dice, I assumed they meant <i>sets</i> of dice, which seems to me like the only quantity of stunt dice that anything lets you spend. But this makes it look like they mean individual dice each time. Huh.<br /> <br /> It's used on Step 4, so it looks to me like <b>Shield of Destiny</b> can be enhanced with an Excellency. Worth remembering when we reach Antagonists, but my guess is that nothing short of an outright bossfight is immune. Think about all the poor schmucks spending 2m to raise their defenses, when a Sidereal does the same thing to become totally immune to an attack <i>and</i> potentially hurt an enemy. This may be the strongest combat Charm I've seen so far (especially if we don't include Abyssals, which I only skimmed but seem to have an auto-kill attack).<br /> <br /> Man, remember back in 2E, when <b>Unswerving Juggernaut Principle</b> seemed to imply you should track movement right down to the single-digit degrees of a turn? Never let my nitpicking in these threads distract from what an improvement we're looking at. Anyway, this Charm is beyond badass.<br /> <br /> See, <b>Shun the Smiling Lady</b> has mechanisms for both the target and other impacted people to resist. That's like 40% of what I'm worried about in the Getimian powers right there.<br /> <br /> <br /> This seems like a good distillation of Sidereal Charms into a very small space. I have more questions than I did for Infernals or Lunars, but not nearly as many as I had for Getimians - I feel like I could run almost all of these in play without any problems. I do wonder how many of Sids' famously oddly placed Charms have been moved to more &quot;normal&quot; Abilities - I only noticed Transcendent Hatchet of Fate going from Lore/Sagacity to Ranged Combat, but I think there were more. I did find it odd that there are no Essence 5 effects, and only a single Essence 4 one (repurchasing Sculpting the Wild Lands into an unnamed Neighborhood Relocation Scheme) - even without Charm trees existing, the Sidereal ones appear to remain closed.<br /> <br /> It always seemed odd to me how the &quot;spy&quot; Exalts had tiny Personal pools which forced them to flare Anima a lot, and for better or worse, Essence very deliberately keeps that contradiction. On the upside, this also shows that the Greater Signs really are meant to be a fairly-regular part of a Sidereal toolbox.<br /> <br /> I think that if I came to this charmset without existing prejudices about Sidereals (fat chance), I would see that they're very sneaky, and good at getting indirect or massive-scale effects - that is, I suppose, the strength of the much-vaunted &quot;best Charm set of 1E,&quot; courtesy of master of strange and large-scale effects Jenna Moran. I would also notice that many of their strongest effects also pointed at long-term consequences you might not like, which is a very cool and subtle thing to get across in a format like this. However, I would probably also be thinking that combat is a bigger part of their themes than it is for Lunars or Getimians (though not Infernals), since those guys had few or highly-specialized combat tricks, while Sidereals get versatile powers that anyone would want to use, such as Shield of Destiny and Unswerving Juggernaut Principle, and that is probably not the intention.<br /> <br /> I try to mostly play support-based characters in RPGs, and just as it was fifteen years earlier, these Sids make a subtle support character seem like the coolest person in the setting. This is my favorite of the Charmsets I've read in-depth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T13:11:14-07:00","id":1452682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452677#post1452677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend to agree (as I said in the post you yourself are quoting, I think it's clear that the intent is Integrity Excellency helping with Resolve), but it is worth noting that the text doesn't establish <i>any</i> requirements for boosting a static value with an Excellency. As written, JohnDoe is correct that any Excellency can boost any static value.</div> </div> </div> </div>It follows the same rules as adding dice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Add that Ability as a dice bonus to an applicable roll involving the chosen Ability. You may add Close Combat dice to Close Combat attacks, or add Integrity dice to Integrity rolls to resist the sway of a Deathlord, but may not use Stealth dice to add to a Close Combat attack or Ranged Combat to add dice to a Navigation roll. </div> </div> </div>So, you can't use Close Combat for Resolve because Resolve is keyed to Integrity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T13:35:07-07:00","id":1452686,"title":"","content":"I reported most &quot;Project&quot; that seemed to be versioning error of the new Venture mechanic.<br /> <br /> Overall I was pleasantly surprised with the Sidereals that I liked much more than the Getimians. I'm still curious as to how they get to Heaven without a chosen of Journey, however","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T13:37:56-07:00","id":1452687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452666#post1452666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree it is a bit redundant yeah but from the looks of it OBS allows you to pick up artifact armor without actually needing armor so if your concept is a bare-chested brawler of invincible might its probably for that but yeah</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. I'm just looking at it and thinking, &quot;who's going to really want Fists of Iron who won't also want Orichalcum Battle Soul?&quot; Maybe it's just me, but very few people who want to play the &quot;unarmed martial artist&quot; don't also want to play them unarmored, which means that OBS will almost always feel mandatory for the Solar brawler/wuxia hero. I see this playing out a few different ways;<br /> <br /> 1) Weapon tags and weight categories aren't a huge deal (to everyone, at least) and fighting for your virtues/intimacies is relatively easy to justify, so plenty of solars interested in punching and kicking things just opt for OBS.<br /> <br /> 2) Weapon tags and weight aren't a huge deal, but for whatever reason justifying your virtues and intimacies is a headache. This seems unlikely to me unless you have a storyteller who really wants to be a stickler about this. You end up buying both, mostly relying on just OBS except when you need to cover the gaps with FoI.<br /> <br /> 3) Weapon Tags or (perhaps more likely) weight categories are a huge help, so people likely take FoI and OBS unless their potential martial arts style specifically says they can't. This ends up feeling a bit redundant, but the possible additional power (even if it's only situational) from FoI makes it worth it.<br /> <br /> Hmmm . . . now that I think about this more, this is probably not a huge issue. Exalted do need to invest a fair bit into their artifact weapons to support their armed fighting styles.<br /> <br /> Artifact sword guy buys his daiklaive with a merit and a charm to never be able to be disarmed. Kung-Fu Gal already has a weapon that can't be disarmed and buys a charm to make it as powerful as an artifact sword. She doesn't get any artifact powers from it, but that's probably a fair trade-off considering her reduced investment. She also gets to learn presumably most of the MA in the setting with her flexible unarmed fighting style . . . I'll be very excited to see both the martial arts charms as well as the artifact weapon examples to see how well these things align.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5849-whiskey-jack","name":"Whiskey Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T14:06:19-07:00","id":1452692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452686#post1452686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I reported most &quot;Project&quot; that seemed to be versioning error of the new Venture mechanic.<br /> <br /> Overall I was pleasantly surprised with the Sidereals that I liked much more than the Getimians. I'm still curious as to how they get to Heaven without a chosen of Journey, however</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think &quot;project&quot; shows up more in the text, so maybe &quot;venture&quot; is the outdated version? I'm using the terms interchangeably for now, but yeah, it could use some clearing up.<br /> <br /> Regarding getting to Heaven, I assume the portals still exist, but it's true that this would probably a bit of a mystery from Essence alone...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T14:48:02-07:00","id":1452695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452681#post1452681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think <b>Last Vision</b> is new, and I secretly hope it was created explicitly so that we can all solve the murder of Sesus Lahor, now that the spiders won't tell. It does, otherwise, feel like a very odd choice for a Sidereal Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div> I believe it's been a Resplendency of the College of the Crow in earlier editions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Cash and Murder Games</b> keeps the awesome name while getting rid of the creepiest language and effects. That makes me very happy, so I feel a little bad that I'm now wondering if this now requires the Sidereal to be in the same place as both targets at once, and if not, what that means for any other Charms which create new influence actions if they don't give details on range - and Essence almost never does. </div> </div> </div> Meanwhile, I'm hoping it has just been made more accessible for XS, and that it isn't a change that will be repeated in 3e. Sidereal Socialize is and should remain about <i>uneven</i> relationships, in accordance with the College of the Lover. The XS version, while fine, seems more like a Charm of the Pillar (and so doesn't really warrant a name like Cash and Murder Games).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 06-17-2021, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T15:08:49-07:00","id":1452700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452695#post1452695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I believe it's been a Resplendency of the College of the Crow in earlier editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it was. I wonder why they thought that &quot;Reading Dead Eyes&quot; was a name that needed changing? I do want to believe they still have to eat an eyeball, however. Builds character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Meanwhile, I'm hoping it has just been made more accessible for XS, and that it isn't a change that will be repeated in 3e. Sidereal Socialize is and should remain about <i>uneven</i> relationships, in accordance with the College of the Lover. The XS version, while fine, seems more like a Charm of the Pillar (and so doesn't really warrant a name like Cash and Murder Games). </div> </div> </div>Text supporting uneven relationships does play into Sid themes, and isn't a bad idea in theory. In practice, this is a quote from printed <i>rules text</i> which I do not feel comfortable relaying without a TRIGGER WARNING for sexual violence:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manual of Exalted Power, Volume 3, The Sidereals</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The victim might fear the beneficiary, desire her sexually, revere her or otherwise define himself in terms of her. (The Sidereal can name herself the beneficiary in such a relationship.) Regardless, the victim cannot resist succumbing to the beneficiary\u2019s will.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That wording is a big problem. I'm not convinced that changing the wording without changing the effect is enough to fix said problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T16:04:00-07:00","id":1452707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452700#post1452700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do want to believe they still have to eat an eyeball, however. Builds character.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, good, I didn't just confabulate that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That wording is a big problem. I'm not convinced that changing the wording without changing the effect is enough to fix said problem. </div> </div> </div> Mm, I disagree. All you have to do is turn it away from the sexual and submissive angle in favour of things like unpaid debts and unrequited love. As long as it gives one party leverage over the other, it's golden.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452654#post1452654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Biggest miss imo for Essence Lunars is them missing Regen charm which has been part of them and talked a lot ....<br /> Not even one at all.... And it saddens me that they totally butchered Lunar Regen characters</div> </div> </div> </div> The Lunar Mode of Body Mending Meditiation helps, but not by much. Definitely a gap in the Charmset, especially next to all the Liminal Meat Energy (they have four different Charms that can heal them or recover/negate Dramatic Injuries).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T16:40:21-07:00","id":1452714,"title":"","content":"It's unfortunate that there don't seem to be the same thematic purviews previous editions had. Some abilities seem to have 4 maidens in the ability. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452700#post1452700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That wording is a big problem. I'm not convinced that changing the wording without changing the effect is enough to fix said problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>The charm is about an unequal relationship flowering up the language doesn't change the nature of the effect. How characters use it determines what it does though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T17:08:58-07:00","id":1452716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452700#post1452700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it was. I wonder why they thought that &quot;Reading Dead Eyes&quot; was a name that needed changing? I do want to believe they still have to eat an eyeball, however. Builds character.</div> </div> </div> </div>In one of the Pathcasts Monica and Dixie stated that it was a design goal to have charms stick to around three words as well as actually describe what they do. Long enough to still be flowery, short enough to fit on a shit.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T21:28:18-07:00","id":1452736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452716#post1452716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one of the Pathcasts Monica and Dixie stated that it was a design goal to have charms stick to around three words as well as actually describe what they do. Long enough to still be flowery, short enough to fit on a shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I had heard that. That's why I was surprised when one of the very few name changes I noticed was to cut a descriptive three-word name. Why does that get the axe, but not Of Truths Best Unspoken, Spider-Amid-Roses Discernment, Rose-Among-Thorns Distinction (no relation), and of course Cash and Murder Games.<br /> <br /> Also, I still need to do in-depth reads of the other Charmsets, but why is Rose-Among-Thorns Distinction even here? In the streamlined ruleset where one Charm is 2-4 normal 3E Charms, why would we possibly have one which is <i>exclusively</i> for infiltrating a group of criminals which you're not actually loyal to? It that a really common Dragonblooded theme? We couldn't have something suited to infiltration or hiding Intimacies in general, we had to get an ability that seemed narrow back in default 3E, then make it even narrower by not even letting it occasionally get you a bonus on a dice roll? That's not quite Refracted Light Analysis-level bad, but I'd still advise virtually anyone to avoid buying it.<br /> <br /> (But if it is here, it could at least be Rose-Among-Thorns <i>Disguise</i>. It's about hiding - the whole point is to remain <i>indistinct</i>!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":2168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","user":"Chejop Kejak","date":". 06-18-2021, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T04:25:32-07:00","id":1452750,"title":"","content":"So far one of the charms i most disagree with is <b>Technique-From-Taste Approach</b>. It sets a very bad precedent as a charm design.<br /> <br /> &quot;When using a mundane item or construct from this discipline, ask the Storyteller any of the following, spending one mote per question:<br /> - How can this be repaired?<br /> - How can this be improved?<br /> - How can this be replicated?&quot; <br /> <br /> Asking questions to ST is the fundamental way we play the game. It should never be a charm. What happens when a dragon blooded, heck forget about DB, what happens when a mortal blacksmith character tries to ask these questions. Either ST will answer them strait up (that is who you play the game afterall) which will make the player that purchased this charm feels like he wasted this xp, or worse after reading this charm ST might answer to the player as &quot;You have to purchase a charm to ask that question&quot; or &quot;You dont have anymore motes to ask questions&quot;. <br /> <br /> Anohter stupid point, as ST you can still answer these questions as &quot; you dont know, you dont understand the intricacies...etc&quot;, nowhere in the charm it states that the ST has to answer.<br /> <br /> I understand the design intent of the charm but the wording is really bad. It should be &quot; ...by spending one mote, you discover the best way to repair/improve/replicate the item/construct.&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T04:41:45-07:00","id":1452751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452750#post1452750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far one of the charms i most disagree with is <b>Technique-From-Taste Approach</b>. It sets a very bad precedent as a charm design.<br /> <br /> &quot;When using a mundane item or construct from this discipline, ask the Storyteller any of the following, spending one mote per question:<br /> - How can this be repaired?<br /> - How can this be improved?<br /> - How can this be replicated?&quot;<br /> <br /> Asking questions to ST is the fundamental way we play the game. It should never be a charm. What happens when a dragon blooded, heck forget about DB, what happens when a mortal blacksmith character tries to ask these questions. Either ST will answer them strait up (that is who you play the game afterall) which will make the player that purchased this charm feels like he wasted this xp, or worse after reading this charm ST might answer to the player as &quot;You have to purchase a charm to ask that question&quot; or &quot;You dont have anymore motes to ask questions&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anohter stupid point, as ST you can still answer these questions as &quot; you dont know, you dont understand the intricacies...etc&quot;, nowhere in the charm it states that the ST has to answer.<br /> <br /> I understand the design intent of the charm but the wording is really bad. It should be &quot; ...by spending one mote, you discover the best way to repair/improve/replicate the item/construct.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The wordings on many charms are quite confusing, and you have to be very charitable to interpret in the intended way, which causes lots of issues of interpretation.<br /> <br /> On my end, rereading DB Anima stuff from Chapter 2, I can't tell how this is supposed to work. Do you roll on your turn ? Each turn you are exposed to it ? Only the first time the DB get over 5 anima ? etc ...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T05:20:59-07:00","id":1452761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452750#post1452750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far one of the charms i most disagree with is <b>Technique-From-Taste Approach</b>. It sets a very bad precedent as a charm design.<br /> <br /> Asking questions to ST is the fundamental way we play the game. It should never be a charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is going to sound a little odd coming from me, but I think this may be a case where you should accept that you're not on the same page as the writers.<br /> <br /> EE is packed full of &quot;ask the ST a question&quot; abilities. Usually (like in the Sidereal &quot;Auspicious [Caste] Insights&quot; abilities), the text specifies that the answers must be useful, or &quot;always reveal at least one clue,&quot; or similar wordings. But sometimes they don't, and even I have a hard time believing that any ST who wasn't going to screw you over anyway would blank all of those character options through asinine answers. Unwoven Coadjutor, Wickedness-Unveiling Method, Celestial Overseer Concordat, Of Truths Best Unspoken, Meditation on Rivalry, General of the All-Seeing Sun, and Strawmaiden's Calling all technically just allow a player to ask a question (sometimes, they don't even specify the ST - Imagine a game making you use a Charm just to ask another player their thoughts!), without ensuring any kind of answer. Heck, the &quot;detective&quot; Universal Charms ensure an honest answer, but don't specify &quot;useful&quot; as some other Charms do, so the ST can still follow your lead and say &quot;you don't know&quot; every time.<br /> <br /> Seeing it all laid out like this, there are even more ST question Charms than I had thought, so I wonder if cutting some of the duplicate wordings about honesty/usefulness would free up the wordcount to put a sidebar very early in the Universal Charms and call out the overall expectations here. It would also be really nice to have a few sentences in the ST section about making sure those powers are useful (even when the player doesn't ask the big, obvious question you planned for and focuses on something else), while also keeping some sense of mystery - but I know darn well they didn't have space for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T08:21:48-07:00","id":1452781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452761#post1452761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seeing it all laid out like this, there are even more ST question Charms than I had thought, so I wonder if cutting some of the duplicate wordings about honesty/usefulness would free up the wordcount to put a sidebar very early in the Universal Charms and call out the overall expectations here. It would also be really nice to have a few sentences in the ST section about making sure those powers are useful (even when the player doesn't ask the big, obvious question you planned for and focuses on something else), while also keeping some sense of mystery - but I know darn well they didn't have space for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you said this very well. The Design Intent behind these Charms is very clearly laid out that the answers <i>must</i> be correct and useful. Yes, there are editing concerns where this is not spelled out on every Charm, but the Intent is very clear. As a ST, this can help me because I will know if/whether the characters have these Charms (or are likely to gain them), and I can prepare answers for game-relevant uses. As a player, as you and Ncolic mention, the only real value of these Charms is the <i>certain </i>knowledge that what you have is correct and useful. As a player, were I in a game where a ST stonewalled the use of these Charms, I would rapidly search for another game to join.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T08:34:12-07:00","id":1452785,"title":"","content":"There's also a speed factor to using the charm. Poke around at a device for an action and then ask your questions. Someone without the charm would take a lot longer to figure those things out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T09:04:35-07:00","id":1452788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452781#post1452781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a ST, this can help me because I will know if/whether the characters have these Charms (or are likely to gain them), and I can prepare answers for game-relevant uses... As a player, were I in a game where a ST stonewalled the use of these Charms, I would rapidly search for another game to join.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness to all the STs out there, I think there will be a reasonably tough period of adjusting to these effects, especially for someone coming from a background of lower-powered RPGs which don't expect the players to be able to simply bypass a mystery. For one thing, even if you do review all of the players' Charms and such before the first session (which is obviously desirable, but not always possible), it's easy to forget or overlook one or two. For another, answers which are helpful, but not total gimmies can be hard to improvise.<br /> <br /> To pick an example from somebody else's actual campaign, so that I'm not just deliberately imagining trouble*, in the Slack-based campaign of Vance's which people could read the logs of, the very first session had the PCs run into a very over-the-top sea captain. He was definitely something unusual, and the PCs were somewhat suspicious about his general deal. In actual play, they didn't have any good leads (and needed to scheme against the Satrap), so they parted ways and he didn't show up again for many sessions, at which point he turned out to be an exiled Raksha noble with a crew of loyal mortals which he (allegedly) only ever Banquet of Crumbs'd, seeking allies to overthrow his own usurper. (Technically, in the game itself, they never verified any of that, so maybe he was lying, but let's work with it.)<br /> <br /> But what if there had been a Chosen of Secrets in the mix! For the low cost of <i>literally nothing</i>, they would probably have turned to the ST and asked &quot;what's the biggest crime this guy has committed recently?&quot; In that position, I would probably struggle: even if feeding on willing humans is illegal (and they were in Realm territory, so it probably was), he does that out at sea on nobody's territory, making the matter hazy. I could improvise some normal Roguish Captain sort of thing (smuggling ten talents worth of opium away from House Cynis, say), but that feels like a total cheat when there is supernatural Shady Stuff going on. And I don't want to spend too long thinking about this, because that would both tip my hand that there's some big reveal here, and slow down play.<br /> <br /> Having typed all of that out, I think the best answer would be to list a not-soul-eating crime... but one which obviously requires supernatural means: &quot;he stole a ten-ton stone idol which the Immaculate Order had slated for destruction, and it's in his ship's hold right now!&quot; I took a minute or two to get there, which could be rough at the table, but suppose I took your advice and came up with it in advance. At that point, I'm groovy... unless the player instead asked &quot;what's this guy's field of expertise,&quot; and I don't want to be as bland as &quot;leadership,&quot; but also don't want to just blurt out &quot;he's an expert at BEING A SOUL-EATING TRICKSTER FAIRY, ALRIGHT?!&quot;<br /> <br /> It's worth repeating that for Sidereals, the first question is free. The game is functionally encouraging them to ping <i>every named NPC</i> in this way. That's a lot of preparation, even without getting into the weeds of whether you can ever &quot;meet&quot; the same person twice, and if so, how long you must be away.<br /> <br /> To be clear, I really like the &quot;ask the ST&quot; effects, and think they're good designs, especially for compacting down the wide range of information-gathering powers Exalts can have into a reasonable amount of space. But this whole rant is my long-winded way of saying: as a player, if you have a few questions whiff, try to be understanding. Maybe talk to your ST between sessions about how your expectations for those effects aren't matching up with theirs. Maybe they'll try to give answers more like you're looking for, or maybe they'll awkwardly tell you that they don't know if they can juggle that mental load along with running the game and ask you to make some other build choice, but either one is probably worth a try before you start seeking a new group.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * Deliberately Imagining Trouble really feels like it should be a Charm name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T10:31:00-07:00","id":1452802,"title":"","content":"Some of the charms so far I've seen, other than the really undertuned ones, are mostly fun. But I think the Getimian's Summoned From Time has some drastic setting implications, even if it's a player only Charm. Not really sure what to think about it because I really do like how cool it can be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T12:04:45-07:00","id":1452807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Distant Choir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452802#post1452802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the charms so far I've seen, other than the really undertuned ones, are mostly fun. But I think the Getimian's Summoned From Time has some drastic setting implications, even if it's a player only Charm. Not really sure what to think about it because I really do like how cool it can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think the setting implications are pretty amazing, actually. Getimians are supposed to be both recent additions to the setting, like the return of the solars, and something that should be a great concern for sidereals and the bureau of destiny. Effects like this cement why. Imagine being a chosen of battles and a getimian fighting guerilla battles against the bureau suddenly shows up with an army from outside of fate. That's exactly the reason they've got to actually deal with this threat.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5849-whiskey-jack","name":"Whiskey Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T13:07:47-07:00","id":1452812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Distant Choir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452802#post1452802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the charms so far I've seen, other than the really undertuned ones, are mostly fun. But I think the Getimian's Summoned From Time has some drastic setting implications, even if it's a player only Charm. Not really sure what to think about it because I really do like how cool it can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly think it's an issue but I think getimians diverge from the setting too extremely for my taste and I don't think I'll use them at all. In my opinion, they do break the no time travel rule by inserting beings from another timeline. Something that i feel is a core ethos of exalted, which is no takes backs which I extend to alternate timelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T13:38:17-07:00","id":1452816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whiskey Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452807#post1452807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually think the setting implications are pretty amazing, actually. Getimians are supposed to be both recent additions to the setting, like the return of the solars, and something that should be a great concern for sidereals and the bureau of destiny. Effects like this cement why. Imagine being a chosen of battles and a getimian fighting guerilla battles against the bureau suddenly shows up with an army from outside of fate. That's exactly the reason they've got to actually deal with this threat.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The army part is interesting and super cool, but it's more the &quot;allies&quot; thing that I'm concerned about since...you can summon Exalts. Celestial Exalts. Gods, armies and wholesale organisations are manageable but Exalts are actually a little too crazy in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T13:41:59-07:00","id":1452817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Distant Choir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452816#post1452816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The army part is interesting and super cool, but it's more the &amp;quot;allies&amp;quot; thing that I'm concerned about since...you can summon Exalts. Celestial Exalts. Gods, armies and wholesale organisations are manageable but Exalts are actually a little too crazy in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing percludes the formerly dead either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T13:53:00-07:00","id":1452818,"title":"","content":"The formerly dead don't seem like a problem to me, because you don't get the original person back, you get someone else with their face - not so different from a Liminal or binding a ghost into a sorcerous clone of their body or whatever.<br /> <br /> Introducing new Celestial Exalts to Creation does raise some big questions. Maybe not in terms of game balance - they're explicitly identical to the Allies Merit, so they would have their own motives and want you to do things for them and have total existential crises about being pulled away from the only Creation they ever knew and so forth.<br /> <br /> But in terms of metaphysics, even if these Exalts don't reincarnate, that's probably a game changer. My inclination would be to assume this has never happened in the past, and if a PC manages to keep a Origin Exalt around long-term, that's a total shock to everyone in-universe, and can drive some interesting stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T14:01:59-07:00","id":1452819,"title":"","content":"That wouldn't be true if the heroic thing the getimian did was save someone who should be dead. It would literally be the same person with just a few different memories. While I'm sure it can be used for insteresting stories I feel it breaks the setting way too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T14:27:00-07:00","id":1452822,"title":"","content":"I guess that I might feel the need to veto a player's background if they went out of their way to make it clear to me their Getimian was Exalted mere moments after saving the life of a semi-major setting figure who was otherwise a complete stranger to them?<br /> <br /> Or I might say &quot;yes,&quot; but still play the NPC as not being the same. Identity is complicated! I realize that many works of fiction have trained us to pretend that an alternate universe version of a dead character can just step into their life with nary a ripple, but I'd rather talk about how this one hates the music the original loved, goes jogging each day out of a grim devotion to training rather than for unbridled enjoyment, and obsessively nicknames everybody rather than speaking formally. Their skills and the events of their life stay the same, but people try to get the Origin version to pick up where the Creation one left off, they're basically descending into one of those psychological thrillers where an abusive weirdo tries to mold the ingenue into replacing their dead lover/child/sibling.<br /> <br /> If anything, my bigger roleplaying concern is why anyone save the most utterly fanatical servant of the Getimian would come through Summoned From Time without <i>hating</i> their former hero for ripping them away from their entire world. Even if this is pitched as step one of a King Radical plan to overwrite the entire world, that's a hell of thing... and if it <i>isn't</i> sold as that, it looks suspiciously like slaughtering your allies' entire families.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T15:27:15-07:00","id":1452825,"title":"","content":"Especially strange when you start considering that the getiminian has to explain that the world they &quot;come from&quot; doesn't actually exist, and maybe never did. Depends on how the lore for them really shakes out (though I actually prefer it stay vague). I honestly like the Getimian more as antagonists for Sidereals than protagonists in their own right. I think that exalts empowered by Sach and Oramus were always going to have abilities that really bent the rules of the setting, nearly to the breaking point. While the power of manifesting a full blown exalt into creation is definitely up there (if not mechanically, then narratively), manifesting an aborted timeline version of a dead person isn't really anymore of a resurrection than wild-shaping a copy of them with a new soul and all the right memories. Part of maintaining the sacred cow is making sure that, in the story, the distinctions that keep it from being a resurrection are boldly highlighted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5849-whiskey-jack","name":"Whiskey Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T17:31:21-07:00","id":1452835,"title":"","content":"I just want to be sure that I am interpreting the way that multiple attack charms (Like Many Attacks Technique) are applied. The charm says that you pay its cost in Step 1, which means that your first attack will not be able to benefit from an Excellency or other charms that also need to be activated on Step 1.<br /> <br /> To me, I think this is a bit unfair for characters that focus on such tactics. I would probably move this to Step 8 so that once an attack is resolved, the Exalt can choose to launch a second attack or wait hold and possibly make a counter attack if they are attacked. This allows both attacks to benefit from other charms in Step 1 (such as using an Excellency for both or whatever). Given the limit on &quot;actions&quot; per round (and that an attack is always considered an action), it seems a little unfair to prevent someone from enhancing two attacks while allowing them to enhance both an an attack and a counterattack (depending if they choose to attack twice or to save one for a potential counter attack).<br /> <br /> Would this change (even if only a house rule) break the balance of combat? Sorry if this has already been discussed, but I couldn't find it discussed earlier in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T18:00:52-07:00","id":1452837,"title":"","content":"A little early to say if it would break the balance of the game or not, but it would certainly shift it. I hadn't really thought about applying excellencies with those yet, but your interpretation makes sense. The only other reading is that you activate the charm in step 1 of the attack that it creates, which is unintuitive to say the least. My personal take is that multiple attacks have always been strong. Magical flurries have been the default combat tactic in every edition of exalted until something crops up to specifically counter them. I like the idea that there's a tradeoff to using extra attack charms. I think they'll still be good, especially with things like excellent strike to cancel the penalty and enhance the attack without relying on an excellency. There might just be other valid fighting styles now, the aforementioned counterattacks being a good contender for another strong thing you can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5849-whiskey-jack","name":"Whiskey Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T19:22:37-07:00","id":1452845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whiskey Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452837#post1452837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A little early to say if it would break the balance of the game or not, but it would certainly shift it. I hadn't really thought about applying excellencies with those yet, but your interpretation makes sense. The only other reading is that you activate the charm in step 1 of the attack that it creates, which is unintuitive to say the least. My personal take is that multiple attacks have always been strong. Magical flurries have been the default combat tactic in every edition of exalted until something crops up to specifically counter them. I like the idea that there's a tradeoff to using extra attack charms. I think they'll still be good, especially with things like excellent strike to cancel the penalty and enhance the attack without relying on an excellency. There might just be other valid fighting styles now, the aforementioned counterattacks being a good contender for another strong thing you can do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Excellent strike does not cancel the penalty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>XS Chapter 4, Flurries</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">This penalty cannot be reduced or ignored unless an effect specifically states so. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T19:55:05-07:00","id":1452849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whiskey Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452837#post1452837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A little early to say if it would break the balance of the game or not, but it would certainly shift it. I hadn't really thought about applying excellencies with those yet, but your interpretation makes sense. The only other reading is that you activate the charm in step 1 of the attack that it creates, which is unintuitive to say the least. My personal take is that multiple attacks have always been strong. Magical flurries have been the default combat tactic in every edition of exalted until something crops up to specifically counter them. I like the idea that there's a tradeoff to using extra attack charms. I think they'll still be good, especially with things like excellent strike to cancel the penalty and enhance the attack without relying on an excellency. There might just be other valid fighting styles now, the aforementioned counterattacks being a good contender for another strong thing you can do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given what appears to be a hard limitation of only two attacks per round, plus the high cost of extra attack charms (well... high for ExEss with Many-Attack Technique costing 2 motes), I would say that this charm isn't too powerful... especially when compared to the counterattack charm Swift Counterattack. Both are viable combat strategies (I can definitely see a fighting concept where an Exalt focuses on blocking attacks made towards him and then counterattacking such attacks). In the end, I think I will house-rule this particular charm to activate on Step 8... thus a character that has both a multi-attack and a counterattack charm will need to choose which to use at this step on a given turn/round. In theory, I don't see this as breaking combat balance over all... just wanted to see if anyone could see anything I might have missed that might potentially cause problems.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your reply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T20:50:08-07:00","id":1452852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452845#post1452845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Excellent strike does not cancel the penalty.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oof, so it is! Thanks for the correction. Still reading and rereading it all. The details haven't all stuck yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5849-whiskey-jack","name":"Whiskey Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T04:19:33-07:00","id":1452883,"title":"","content":"Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Style...alright I like that only Sidereals get the full mastery bonus of SMA style. Solars (All variants included) and Getimians can learn SMA from Sidereal tutors. Meanwhile, the door is open for Terrestrial exalted to learn them by Story event chosen by the storyteller and player instead of mechanics (I enjoy this bit, might be a way to help out terrestrial exalted in mixed chronicles later on).<br /> <br /> I enjoy that there some distinct limit of what kind of circle of Sorcery and Necromancy each exalted and Supernatural beings type can achieve. Abyssal and Solar mirroring each other (Third circle for one and Second circle for the other). Only Deathlords and Abyssals can use Third Circle Necromancy...compared to Incarna, direct Fetich souls, Solars (and Infernals) who can use Third Circle Sorcery.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T04:50:47-07:00","id":1452885,"title":"","content":"I have the feeling the MA are a bit underwhelming, but maybe it's because I haven't tested the fighting system yet. I have a player that wants to play a Water DB Martial Artist and he was expecting the Water Style to come. I won't say it's just straight bad, but with 5 Charms only at the beginning I have the feeling he's better served with an Excellency rather than the First Charm of Water MA. Maybe I'm wrong though, we might need to see","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T06:38:28-07:00","id":1452889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452885#post1452885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the feeling the MA are a bit underwhelming, but maybe it's because I haven't tested the fighting system yet. I have a player that wants to play a Water DB Martial Artist and he was expecting the Water Style to come. I won't say it's just straight bad, but with 5 Charms only at the beginning I have the feeling he's better served with an Excellency rather than the First Charm of Water MA. Maybe I'm wrong though, we might need to see</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I read of the MAs, they are good. Them having limited charms is on purpose and with how complimentary abilities work you can't just invest in one thing for MAs. As for investing at the start, yeah its likely inadvisable to do that but thats fine. What effects water does have though sound very fun","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T06:59:30-07:00","id":1452891,"title":"","content":"My first takeaways from reading through the Martial Arts chapters<br /> <br /> 1) I really like this method of martial arts prerequisites and form weapon restrictions. It does a great job of giving styles an identity while allowing for an atypical practitioner to wield a strange weapon and still work.<br /> <br /> 2) A few charms talk about setting soak to half fortitude rounded down. Everyone has a base soak of 1, and already gains an extra point if their fortitude is 4 or higher. . . am I missing something? If armor and/or the physique bonus are applied after, the charms (water dragon form is one) could definitely be clearer on this.<br /> <br /> 3) Speaking of form weapons, Water Dragon Style lists piercing as one of its tags, which spears will presumably have. This might mean that Peleps Deled can actually use that dire lance with his martial art now . . .<br /> <br /> EDIT: because I misremembered physique contributing to soak instead of fortitude (which I thought was odd). I'm now assuming the intended interaction is supposed to be that you get the extra point of soak for high physique after setting your base to two and still gain bonuses from armor, but that interaction does not seem obvious to me on first read. Maybe I'd feel differently reading this fresh and not coming into it with preconceptions from earlier editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5849-whiskey-jack","user":"Whiskey Jack","date":". 06-19-2021, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5849-whiskey-jack","name":"Whiskey Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T07:46:14-07:00","id":1452894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whiskey Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452891#post1452891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) A few charms talk about setting soak to half fortitude rounded down. Everyone has a base soak of 1, and already gains an extra point if their fortitude is 4 or higher. . . am I missing something? If armor and/or the physique bonus are applied after, the charms (water dragon form is one) could definitely be clearer on this.<br /> <br /> EDIT: because I misremembered physique contributing to soak instead of fortitude (which I thought was odd). I'm now assuming the intended interaction is supposed to be that you get the extra point of soak for high physique after setting your base to two and still gain bonuses from armor, but that interaction does not seem obvious to me on first read. Maybe I'd feel differently reading this fresh and not coming into it with preconceptions from earlier editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm wrong in this, but I was assuming that you were resetting your soak, thus removing any penalties to it. Maybe I'm wrong with that, but I just don't see any other way that could be beneficial if that isn't the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T07:52:34-07:00","id":1452896,"title":"","content":"I haven't read MAs &amp; Sorcery yet, but I do think that the intention is for multiattack Charms to occupy Step 1 of the attack they <i>create</i>.<br /> <br /> The text never says this, but it fits with the pattern: all Charms which do not specify a Step are Step 1 by default, and lots of them create new actions without specifying another Step. For consistency, whenever it's ambiguous, I will be assuming that all Charms which create actions work that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T10:18:16-07:00","id":1452901,"title":"","content":"Okay, Martial Arts time. Sorry, all you splats I keep putting off! It's that I dislike you (well, okay, I do dislike some of you), just that looking at a charm set in this level of detail, with stops for cross-referencing and errata reports, takes like two hours. I'm hoping to do it for all of them, if only because articulating my thoughts well enough to write them out here is a great way to figure out what rules and I do and don't get, as well as what seems outright incorrect.<br /> <br /> (I started on Liminals yesterday, but that will be an even larger investment than average.)<br /> <br /> I think I like the overall approach to MAs here, with Complimentary Skills and weapons defined by tags rather than a list (no more &quot;why does this style allow Seven-Section Staff, but not Fighting Chain&quot;), though it is a little odd that I can now use Close Combat Charms to enhance ranged attacks, but still care about Form weapons. I hope that armor isn't a huge deal for moderately-invested combatants here, the way it is in 3E - massively penalizing random MAs based on what appear to be aesthetic rather than balance concerns is a pet peeve of mine.<br /> <br /> We start with my old archnemesis, Crane Style. It immediately justifies my opinion of it by falling into a version error: the intro talks about the Celestial and Terrestrial tags, but Crane actually uses Mastery (Celestial) and Mastery (Terrestrial). If that means anything, a search cannot tell me what.<br /> <br /> <b>Fluttering Cry Of Warning</b> reveals a baffling detail of the Defend Other rules. It already bugged me that EE was following 3E's lead by making &quot;Defending&quot; an ally actually refer to redirecting all attacks on them towards yourself with functionally no counterplay. But now, I learn there is one way in which this isn't true: Decisive attacks hurt the defender and apply the defender's soak, but apparently they still check the original target's Hardness. Why?<br /> <br /> And while I'm on the subject, what happens the Celestial version of this reflexively raises the target's Hardness high enough that the attack on them is illegal? The Alchemical Charm Reinforced Chassis forces the attacker to switch to Withering, and that's probably what I would do in other cases, but there's no general rule here - one could assume that action is just &quot;wasted,&quot; or that they get to declare a new action with no penalties instead, and those are pretty wide extremes.<br /> <br /> <b>Crane Form</b> does the Crossed Wings Denial thing in a ruleset which actually supports it, which is nice, and I really like that both Modes are such cool wuxia tropes that it makes me sad to not get both - nobody is being shafted here. However, as usual, I am dubious of &quot;this gets massively better when your opponents are opposing your Virtues&quot; stuff. That looks to me like a clause which encourages bad character design - like Alchemical advantages, it pays a player off for picking broad &quot;Path of What I Was Going To Do Anyway&quot; stuff. Almost any Ambition will be &quot;opposed&quot; by anyone who dares try to kill you, but almost no Courage will be (&quot;How dare you run away - my Defense increases by a further point!&quot;), for example.<br /> <br /> Um, <b>Humbling Enlightenment Commentary</b>, you do know that running out of HLs doesn't kill named enemies by default, right? What are even the rules for this &quot;unconscious&quot; situation? Can allies wake them up with a single action, like from the Gambit? Does it have some limited duration? Probably yes and no, respectively, but why do this at all in a world where Incapping is cast in such loose and narrative terms?<br /> <br /> Ninja time!<br /> <br /> Should<b> Nothing But Shadows</b> stack with regular concealment? As written, I think it does not.<br /> <br /> <b>Throat-Slitting Shadow Strike</b> is the first Charm that I've seen where the power difference between Modes is immediately clear. One is a 2-mote swing, which looks pretty huge in Essence... the other is a cool stunt.<br /> <br /> Mantis! Huh, both &quot;defensive, grounded animal Kung Fu&quot; styles in the core.<br /> <br /> Some of <b>Iron-Arm Block</b>'s effects last for one attack, some last until next turn, and one of them (regarding flurry penalties) my be literally impossible to use. Even if I can declare Charms on my own Step 2 (and I sure hope not), that's not when a flurry would be declared.<br /> <br /> I wonder what (Celestial) <b>Mantis Form</b> thinks it means in game terms if it &quot;inflicts a wrenching injury that keeps the opponent from using one of their limbs&quot;? Almost all movement is unrolled, so unless they're using a very two-handed fighting style, the effects seem like they would be entirely narrative (or incredibly harsh for something being made up with no textual support). Maybe they also reduce the Attribute they care about the least by 1, Dramatic Injury style?<br /> <br /> <b>Unfolding Retribution Strike</b> is making me confront the distinction between &quot;contested roll&quot; attacks in a grapple, and clashes. There admittedly <i>is</i> such a distinction, and it seems clear enough to apply, but now I'm wondering why there needs to be. It's kind of quirky how the Celestial mode expects to slowly wear enemies down with a pack of allies, and the Terrestrial one expects to quickly drop the target outright, then gain Power to help with the next one.<br /> <br /> Righteous Devil without having seen the Flame tag seems potentially hard to... <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> ...judge. I outright refuse to believe that this Martial Art associated with a single lore character and a single concept has ever had the 4+ practitioners required for &quot;Creation-spanning rivalr<i>ies</i>,&quot; plural. Interestingly, its only Modes are for Solars and Solars alone.<br /> <br /> Wait, if a character uses (Solar) <b>Blossom of Inevitable Demise</b>, can their side just have her act last in the first round, making interrupts totally impossible until round 2?<br /> <br /> Being stuck in melee against (Solar) <b>Righteous Devil Form</b> looks miserable - they Aim, use their free Excellency, and then blast you with +11 dice, for a total of 22 (plus whatever Accuracy ends up looking like). Against the Charmless maximum Defense of 5, this is a hit with +6 damage dice. They're not even spending motes. Pray they didn't bother with the Close Combat 3 for Excellent Strike.<br /> <br /> I really appreciate the <b>Burning Judgement Halo</b> actually specifies that it doesn't harm the Exalt (and so, by extension, we can reason it's deliberate that it <i>doesn't</i> mention allies being immune to this literal friendly fire), though I am a little surprised by the Solar mode, which appears to easily be the most complex area-based effect I've seen in the game. Hope you brought plenty of post-it motes for those index card &quot;range band&quot; trackers!<br /> <br /> Snake Style, explicitly called out as The Martial Art You Find Everywhere.<br /> <br /> <b>Snake Form</b> actually has rules for disabling parts of the body! Take note, Mantis Form.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts effect sure do seem to love skipping directly from Short to Long Range, between Burning Judgement Halo and <b>Uncoiling Serpent Aura</b>. I was going to say the Celestial Mode looks insanely deadly, assuming that it (and poisons in general) means levels of damage, rather than dice. However, re-reading the rules for poisons, I noticed that &quot;When a character rolls to resist a poison\u2019s damage, she also reduces its duration by the same number of successes,&quot; and now I have much bigger questions about that. The same as <i>what</i>, Essence? Extra successes, extra successes plus one for success, or <i>total</i> successes? The example seems to imply the second option, because it says Mercurial Iris &quot;reduces&quot; the poison's duration, but actually just has it tick down by 1 like it was going to do anyway, and then seems to think that &quot;another successful attempt&quot; will plausibly involve 8+ successes on 8 dice, which is more than a little optimistic.<br /> <br /> My point is that a poison with Damage 3/round, a 3-round duration, and Difficulty 4 is brutal for anyone who didn't build heavily for Fortitude + Physique - 5 levels of damage if you're reasonably lucky, and 9 is a real possibility. And poison resistance rolls seem hard to stunt.<br /> <br /> Tiger Style. It lets you treat Light Form weapons as medium, which could be interesting with some other MAs - most of the ones so far share either Concealable or Disarming.<br /> <br /> I'm honestly a little confused by what ends up Celestial versus Terrestrial. Overall, it seems like Terrestrial ones have larger statistical bonuses, and Celestial ones grant over overall control over the flow of combat. That's already an unexpected place to end up, but then there's cases like the Celestial mode of <b>Tiger Form</b> being almost identical to the Terrestrial Mode of Ebon Shadow Form. What does that mean? Is there any pattern beyond legacy code?<br /> <br /> White Reaper,able for having Lunar modes, and for being not the Martial Art That Is In No Way A Martial Art.<br /> <br /> Oh, you don't believe me? Consider this: <b>White Reaper Form</b> appears to lock Sidereal Characters out of accessing the Greater Signs, since you can't go above Anima 10, and cannot spend Halos on Anima effects. A Martial Art which has anti-synergy with the Martial Artist splat is surely on somewhat shaky ground.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you can finally raise your Resolve in combat, and all you had to do was rip people's souls out with your bare hands.<br /> <br /> (Lunar) <b>Bleeding Crescent Strike</b> doesn't say anything about dividing Power, so can you really use 10 Power against each of four different opponents? I don't know how often you'll ever have that many enemies in melee, but it's still a pretty wild possibility.<br /> <br /> This doesn't have much to do with Martial Arts, but it only occurred to me at this point in my reading that there's no general rule establishing a maximum Hardness. As written, I see nothing to stop you from focusing on defensive tech until you reach Hardness 11 and become immune to Decisive attacks.<br /> <br /> In any case, that took even longer than I expected (we're already at something like 1.5 normal Charmsets, so that may not be too shocking). Next time I'm free, it'll be the Five Dragon Styles, plus the much-hyped one Sidereal Style.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T10:36:02-07:00","id":1452902,"title":"","content":"I personally don't mind the anti-synergy between white-reaper and sidereals' greater signs. The Lunar only modes already drive home the fact that this style has a clear home. Other people can use it, sure, and will still derive some strong benefits, but just like this version of righteous devil, it's not meant to be another kung-fu style under the belt of the sidereal sifu. It fits a more specific niche. Besides, we're getting a good diversity of styles for sidereal sifus, and the five dragon styles look like they'll have good teeth for sidereals even without the dragonblooded only effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5849-whiskey-jack","name":"Whiskey Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T21:07:20-07:00","id":1452920,"title":"","content":"I don't know that it's bad design or anything, but it does reinforce my stereotype that this heavy armored, self-healing, silver aura thing is just the Lunar Melee tree which they normally don't receive. The only things I've ever used it for were as a pre-Fangs Lunar charmset, and to beef out Ahlat.<br /> <br /> Though, typing all of that, I really can't shake the feeling this is an Abyssal thing, with the soul stealing and all.<br /> <br /> But I don't have time to be ambivalent about White Reaper being a corebook style again, because I'm too busy being ambivalent about the Five Dragon Styles being in the corebook. Sure, they're iconic, DBs would feel a little incomplete without them, and some of the most interesting MAs in the game are Dragon Styles... but they're also really heavily pitched towards Dragonblooded and nobody else. I can't quite shake the feeling that if we're going to have 20 pages of Martial Arts, we maybe shouldn't spend one third of them on one tenth of characters. Yes, I know, lore-wise these make some sense for Sidereals, and somebody always wants to play the ex-Immaculate Solar, but Exalt-only Modes feel to me like they would discourage that.<br /> <br /> Mixed feelings, for sure.<br /> <br /> As ever, we start with Air Dragon. Alphabetization at work: we always begin with the oddest, least-representative Style, just because stupid William the Bastard had to get Lyft replaced with some Latin word 700 years ago. Boo.<br /> <br /> Um, anyway. Aid Dragon shows off its oddness right off the bat, as a Style which lets you fight unarmed, but with a special tag effect which only works on their chakrams. Neat.<br /> <br /> I may have to walk back (heh) a little bit of my questioning how many characters will want these, because even modeless <b>Cloud-Treading Method</b> looks like a pretty strong dip for any combat character who meets the prerequisites. A ranged character can kite people all day, a melee one can hit somebody then go two bands away, leaving their target with no appealing options for fighting them.<br /> <br /> The downside is, I thought this was something which could be done already. I went back to movement actions, and Sprint doesn't mention any limitations on flurries... but the section does mention that &quot;some movement actions can be used as part of a combat flurry, which will be stated in the action\u2019s text.&quot; So, &quot;normal&quot; combat action descriptions will only tell you if the <i>cannot</i> be flurried, but movement actions apparently cannot flurry by default, and so only mention if they <i>can</i>. Dammit, Essence, just pick one default case, and mention exceptions to that! Why do you insist on changing the baseline all the time? Why is there a different general rule for counterattacks than for other reflexive actions? Why do you hate straightforward communication?<br /> <br /> I have seldom been more curious whether a Charm was doing dice or levels of damage than I am when reading <b>Wrathful Winds Roar</b>. This can quickly become a Difficulty 5 roll against taking 7+ [somethings] of damage - no Soak, no Defense, if you don't have an Excellency in... whatever Ability you resist this thing with (it's not specified, and there doesn't seem to be a general rule for environmental hazards), you take it. heck, even if you manage to hit Difficulty 5, you're not safe, you reduce the damage by <i>one</i>, then one more for each extra success. If those are levels (and the rules seem to imply they are), this is a death sentence which can easily be dropped on the first or second round.<br /> <br /> (I'm mostly reserving judgement on balance until I actually get some play in, but honestly, this looks insane even if they're damage dice. Maybe Soak somehow applies?)<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon Style next. Interestingly, its weapon tag effect is strictly worse than that of Ebon Shadow.<br /> <br /> The actual Charms of Earth Dragon all seem clear and straightforward. Come to think on it, I feel like that's been true across the editions. It truly is the element of stability.<br /> <br /> Fire Dragon brings back an age-old question: are you dual wielding when you fight unarmed?<br /> <br /> <b>Searing Edge Attack</b> seems pretty bad most of the time. I spend a mote so that someone else <i>might</i> lose one? If you have the mote economy to make this look good, surely you're already way ahead, especially since this is Essence - unlike 3E, a Celestial mote isn't just worth more.<br /> <br /> Blah blah, <b>Fiery Blade Attack</b>, blah blah, want to know about levels versus dice and the resistance pool. I know that in the unlikely event that anybody is reading this, you know the drill.<br /> <br /> Water Dragon implies that Tiger Claws might have the One-Handed tag, which is surprising if true. Also, in the first real surprise of the Complementary Abilities, it uses Sagacity. Sure, What Fire Has Wrought lists Occult, but they <i>all</i> do that.<br /> <br /> I was surprised not to see Bottomless Depths Defense, one of the most famous MA Charms, adapted here, but on reading closer, it looks like that's what the Dragon-Blooded Mode of <b>Water Dragon Form</b> is doing. That's really clever!<br /> <br /> <b>Foe-Restraining Whirlpool</b> marks the second time that the book has talked about losing your Reflexive movement as meaning you &quot;must flurry&quot; rolls to move. So, are you not allowed to <i>just</i> Sprint? Do you have to make a Difficulty 3 roll, even though combat movement in Essence mostly involves no dice rolling? I don't really know whether this is a versioning thing, or I'm just being obtuse. Does anyone have a theory here?<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon sticks to 3E's decision to let them hit people with bows, but not use their Charms through arrows. This, once again, is an edition where I see no obstacle to using Excellent Strike or Ready In Eight Directions with a bow. I do not understand the choice, and would surely houserule it in a game I ran.<br /> <br /> Unlike Water Dragon, &quot;esotericism and medicine&quot; Style getting Sagacity makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> <b>Wood Dragon Form </b>looks unspeakably beefy. Comparing it to, say, Mantis Form, this might be better <i>before</i> you get to healing a level every round.<br /> <br /> &quot;Opponents with Power lower than the Exalt\u2019s Finesse plus one,&quot; <b>Unbreakable Fascination Exercise</b>, really? &quot;Equal or less&quot; seems clearer to me, but okay.<br /> <br /> <b>Soul Mastery</b> looks like a pretty good effort at the eternal challenge of making an instant kill attack neither useless nor broken. I do have to wonder about the &quot;cannot cost more than 10 Power&quot; clause, since the only way I can see for that to happen is if your opponent somehow has Defense 11+, and if that problem comes, that would an issue with or without Soul Mastery.<br /> <br /> I feel like I have a few more doubts about the Immaculate Styles than the earlier ones, often due to inheriting odd legacy ideas like &quot;these styles for a group of martial artists to overwhelm one strong opponent are loaded with area effects which cannot tell friend from foe.&quot; As always, I want to run off and build an Air Style expert who no other player would want to work with (lots of long, grindey fights, lots of running away which would end up abandoning most other PCs), and I think that Earth looks solid but dull, Fire looks gimmickey and useless, Water looks strong but reliant on facing small numbers of &quot;elite&quot; enemies, and have mixed feelings on Wood. The fact that I have the same core reaction to each of these styles as I have in the past definitely shows that Essence remains great at evoking core Exalted themes in a very stripped-down format.<br /> <br /> But, hey, enough about that. We're <i>really</i> here to see how they could have possibly pulled off a Sidereal Style!<br /> <br /> First off, it's a little surprising that the book says Getimians cannot develop these Styles and need direct Sidereal tutelage to learn them. Add that to the list of lines which will be extensively litigated between now and whenever Timmies get their own book.<br /> <br /> &quot;All other targets must flurry an Integrity roll to attack&quot; an Exalt with <b>Games of Divinity Form</b> active, eh? If I'm reading this right, they don't need to succeed on that roll, it just taxes their dice pools and action economy (and makes clashes and counterattacks outright impossible), so maybe that's also the idea with the &quot;no reflexive movement&quot; stuff.<br /> <br /> <b>Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Form</b> definitely does not make it clear to me whether the writers are expecting multiple Forms to stack with each other, or what kind of action they're supposed to take. It doesn't even give me any idea of where &quot;extreme range&quot; ends - I somehow doubt this Charm is meant to let Getimians sense all Essence use in Creation.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, this MA is completed at Essence 3, meaning there are <i>still</i> no high-Essence Charms for Sidereals in Essence.<br /> <br /> Sadly, I'm having some trouble separating my feelings on Essence's take on this style from being reminded of the reasons why I never liked Prismatic Arrangement in the first place. These effects do look powerful, though, and a Getimian mode which explicitly exists to mess up Sidereal abilities is neat.<br /> <br /> Regarding Martial Arts as a whole, I don't know. It's a classic part of Exalted, so there was likely never any question whether it would be here. Most of these Styles are exactly the ones that everyone would guess (I might have expected one of the animal styles to trade out for Dreaming Pearl Courtesan). Even so, I was mostly left with the feeling that these Styles were less widely-useful than the Universal Charms, and less flavorful than the Exalt-specific ones. There are some which carve out unique niches (Righteous Devil, Air Dragon, Crane) or have some degree of minigame (Wood Dragon, White Reaper) that makes these Charms feel like a package deal apart from everything else (unfortunately, most of the ones which stuck out at me are only aimed at a single splat), but overall, I am less excited about most MA Charms than I was the ones which came before, and find myself wondering if they're the reason why some plats' combat suites (especially Getimians) felt so perfunctory. I think I'd probably use them because a character concept called for it, rather than construct a character to justify playing with these cool toys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T21:23:09-07:00","id":1452921,"title":"","content":"Just as a side note, in general, I don't believe that we will see many high essence charms due to the new paradigm of the setting for 3e.<br /> <br /> Most Exalted eventually settle at Essence 3 in their lifetime, a few become elder and reach Essence 4. Essence 5 and higher is exceptional and rare for all exalted in 3e. If high essence charms of some SMA exist, they will probably be charms made by individuals masters/keeping to themselves like the charms of the Elder Lunars in Lunar Fangs at the Gate (some are Essence 6 charms still the power of Essence 5 charms, but more made to be unique to the elder who created it). I would not be surprised for example, if Chejob Kejak has unique martial arts charms just for how long, he has been alive.<br /> <br /> Essentially just saying that Elders don't have a lot of opportunities to share high essence charms with their peers other Elders.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T21:45:13-07:00","id":1452923,"title":"","content":"I don't know if that's true in Essence.<br /> <br /> I do know that Alchemicals, Sidereals, Lunars, and Solars are the only four splats to not get at least one Essence 5 Charm in this book. Solars have four different Essence 5 upgrades, so Alchemicals, Lunars, and Sidereals stand out for having no outright Essence 4-5 Charms (and exactly two Essence 4 upgrades) among them.<br /> <br /> For contrast, Strawmaiden Janest - a unique being who is almost certainly not currently at that level of power - has <i>six</i> Essence 4-5 effects.<br /> <br /> Yes, homebrew is a thing, but for the Exalt types most strongly associated with having active elders to be the very ones which lack elder Charms is a mildly-puzzling writing decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T21:46:41-07:00","id":1452924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452920#post1452920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I have a few more doubts about the Immaculate Styles than the earlier ones, often due to inheriting odd legacy ideas like &quot;these styles for a group of martial artists to overwhelm one strong opponent are loaded with area effects which cannot tell friend from foe.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe area of affect attacks only target enemies by default in Essence, unless they explicitly say otherwise. The definition of attacks says:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Attacks always target enemy characters and cannot be taken against friendly characters \u2014 unless the character is being controlled by an enemy or the story dictates such a thing (like characters fighting in a tournament). </div> </div> </div>I believe in one of the live plays, it was said that Death by Obsidian Butterflies only targets enemies in the area, for example, and I *think* Monica confirmed that area of effect attacks only target enemies.<br /> <br /> I'm less clear about environmental effects that do damage; do they count as attacks for this purpose? Not sure...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26886-lindharin","name":"Lindharin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-19T22:13:48-07:00","id":1452925,"title":"","content":"I would definitely be leery of reading &quot;no, you cannot abuse Withering attacks by using them on an ally who deliberately tanks their Defense&quot; as &quot;everyone you like is totally unharmed when you set the entire area on fire&quot; without some less-ambiguous details.<br /> <br /> Notably, if it were that simple, why would all of these effects specify not hitting the user?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T06:52:05-07:00","id":1452949,"title":"","content":"While the martial arts are understandably rudimentary, and the lone SMA doubly so, there are several things I like in the MAs: the complementary Abilities as actual prereqs, the way learning a Charm alters your unarmed attacks/use of form weapons, and most importantly that the MA Charms <i>actually specify if they supplement withering or decisive attacks.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T10:09:40-07:00","id":1452973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452925#post1452925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would definitely be leery of reading &quot;no, you cannot abuse Withering attacks by using them on an ally who deliberately tanks their Defense&quot; as &quot;everyone you like is totally unharmed when you set the entire area on fire&quot; without some less-ambiguous details.<br /> Notably, if it were that simple, why would all of these effects specify not hitting the user?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that is a good question. I asked for clarification on the discord, and it is the intent that AOE does not hit allies unless it explicitly says otherwise. <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/205962784599441408/652577291318198316/856216130221113344\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the link.</a> <br /> EDIT: Monica also said that whether this applies to environmental effects caused by a player is something that needs clarification, so we don't have an answer for that yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26886-lindharin","user":"Lindharin","date":". 06-20-2021, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26886-lindharin","name":"Lindharin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T11:37:13-07:00","id":1452975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lindharin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452973#post1452973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that is a good question. I asked for clarification on the discord, and it is the intent that AOE does not hit allies unless it explicitly says otherwise. <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/205962784599441408/652577291318198316/856216130221113344\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the link.</a><br /> EDIT: Monica also said that whether this applies to environmental effects caused by a player is something that needs clarification, so we don't have an answer for that yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Thank you for the follow-up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-20T18:44:52-07:00","id":1453004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1452949#post1452949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the martial arts are understandably rudimentary, and the lone SMA doubly so, there are several things I like in the MAs: the complementary Abilities as actual prereqs, the way learning a Charm alters your unarmed attacks/use of form weapons, and most importantly that the MA Charms <i>actually specify if they supplement withering or decisive attacks.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think that PAoC has been shrunk without losing much. The sidereal bonus for PAoC and Games of divinity form seem underwheling though. PAoC's problem in my opinion is that you can apparently just stack form charms now. So just getting one extra seems a little weak. I wish it was back to the original charm if that's the case. Where it was all of PAoC at once or two of any kind. Whereas Games of divinity form's extra successes are kind of lame to putting back in the addiction effect it used to have. <br /> <br /> These are still minor issues though and they could have been done way worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 06-21-2021, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T04:31:37-07:00","id":1453020,"title":"","content":"I don't like how All-Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight can see all forms of essence use again.<br /> <br /> In 2nd edition I regularly encountered PCs who wanted it active permanently and occasionally Storytellers would create these 'null zone' encounters where in order to be discreet the PCs weren't able to spend a mote of essence and had to stash all their artifact gear... which sounded like a challenge on paper but in practice was taking away the Exalt part of Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T05:51:42-07:00","id":1453027,"title":"","content":"3E's All-Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight is pretty narrow, and I've seen people repeatedly be surprised when it doesn't do things they expect it to. Not detecting Exalts is especially baffling, given how trivially low-Essence Spirits can do that, seemingly infallibly unless you use a perfect effect against them.<br /> <br /> That said, I can see the Essence version as being too much of a temptation to just leave on. I think my preferred fix would be to leave the full functionality (Essence is big on both giving PCs information and not letting NPCs play by the same rules as them), but make it spend a mote to turn on AESS for one scene, rather than committing. That way, you only use it when you have a reason to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T06:40:50-07:00","id":1453034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453027#post1453027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3E's All-Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight is pretty narrow, and I've seen people repeatedly be surprised when it doesn't do things they expect it to. Not detecting Exalts is especially baffling, given how trivially low-Essence Spirits can do that, seemingly infallibly unless you use a perfect effect against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's always been a genre thing.<br /> <br /> Potentially hostile Exalts running around with Exalt detectors takes a humongous shit on social, disguise and stealth orientated characters while a field guardian being able to tell that the person walking in their fields is a Solar is more of an opportunity for plot and character development. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T07:12:51-07:00","id":1453036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453034#post1453034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Potentially hostile Exalts running around with Exalt detectors takes a humongous shit on social, disguise and stealth orientated characters while a field guardian being able to tell that the person walking in their fields is a Solar is more of an opportunity for plot and character development.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that works right up until a First Circle Demon sees print with an easy enough Measure The Wind condition. Whether that exists yet in 3E depends largely on how you read the Anhule's need to &quot;hunt&quot; the target, but if there's ever something like the old requirements for Perroneles (anything which poses a danger to its host) or Teodozjia (just smell it), then Exalt detectors are only a Charm away in any case.<br /> <br /> I admittedly don't know whether MtW will be printed in Essence, however, so it might make more sense to me nerfing AESS here than most places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T09:15:04-07:00","id":1453045,"title":"","content":"Looking back at Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Style, I like it better than I did at first blush.<br /> <br /> Stacking up a ton of scenelongs still doesn't strike me as a very exciting way to convey the Ultimate Mastery Of Martial Technique (tm), but since each of the first three Forms only requires E2 and any 3 MA Charms, they have a fair bit of value as pseudo-capstones to the other Styles (Four Magical Materials, in particular, has a range of effects to synergize with whatever MA you chose), or to let someone cherry-pick the first Charm each of three different MAs, take this at E2, and feel like they have a &quot;real&quot; Style, with four Charms including a Form.<br /> <br /> So that's my bad. This definitely justifies its place in the book.<br /> <br /> I do need to figure out what degeneracy Soul Fire Shaper allows, however. Ebon Shadow Form has a couple of effects that scale with Essence, though one is problematically locked behind the Terrestrial keyword. Wrathful Winds Roar is as genuinely upsetting as ever (probably 8 levels/dice when you take it, eventually scaling up to 12). I think the real payoff, though, are over in the Anima abilities, many of which scale by Essence. There's tons of &quot;add (essence) bonus successes&quot; stuff, which is gravy, but really this just lets you hit the &quot;dice&quot; limit at E3 rather than E5. The really scary stuff happens if E5 Alchemicals can learn SMA. Lots of them have powerful abilities based on Essence/2 (rounded up), so Soul Fire does all kinds of stupid stuff, like +4 to attack and damage rolls for your whole side. In the land of the canonically supported, Thousand Tears Elixir and the Greater Sign of Secrets both give out some odd results.<br /> <br /> Of course, most of that is a little debatable as being &quot;static value calculations, rolls, or costs,&quot; which I guess is an escape hatch if anything looks too absurd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T11:24:02-07:00","id":1453057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453045#post1453045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking back at Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Style, I like it better than I did at first blush.<br /> I do need to figure out what degeneracy Soul Fire Shaper allows, however. Ebon Shadow Form has a couple of effects that scale with Essence, though one is problematically locked behind the Terrestrial keyword. Wrathful Winds Roar is as genuinely upsetting as ever (probably 8 levels/dice when you take it, eventually scaling up to 12). I think the real payoff, though, are over in the Anima abilities, many of which scale by Essence. There's tons of &quot;add (essence) bonus successes&quot; stuff, which is gravy, but really this just lets you hit the &quot;dice&quot; limit at E3 rather than E5. The really scary stuff happens if E5 Alchemicals can learn SMA. Lots of them have powerful abilities based on Essence/2 (rounded up), so Soul Fire does all kinds of stupid stuff, like +4 to attack and damage rolls for your whole side. In the land of the canonically supported, Thousand Tears Elixir and the Greater Sign of Secrets both give out some odd results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Active Animas also are mostly converting Essence dice to successes for you and your allies - it's only 1/die per essence for each person, but the area of effect makes it strong, and I don't think caps apply. At essence 5 with Soul Fire Shaper you can automatically get 7 successes on some dice before you roll, and haven't even used any of your cap up.<br /> <br /> A Chosen of Serenity with Attribute 5, Performance 5, the excellency, Greatness-Inspiring Aura and Essence 3 can average 13 successes on a build power action - enough to take someone from 0 to 10 power with 1 left over. Spending only 1m. With room for 3 more dice and 3 more successes if you can find bonuses anywhere<br /> And all of their allies who have Attribute 5 can make 7.5 success build power actions as well, based on GIA and the Serenity Aura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T11:26:24-07:00","id":1453058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453036#post1453036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that works right up until a First Circle Demon sees print with an easy enough Measure The Wind condition. Whether that exists yet in 3E depends largely on how you read the Anhule's need to &quot;hunt&quot; the target, but if there's ever something like the old requirements for Perroneles (anything which poses a danger to its host) or Teodozjia (just smell it), then Exalt detectors are only a Charm away in any case.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd rather attribute anything that allows this to a design oversight rather than something that should be emulated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T11:58:36-07:00","id":1453063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453045#post1453045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking back at Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Style, I like it better than I did at first blush.<br /> <br /> Stacking up a ton of scenelongs still doesn't strike me as a very exciting way to convey the Ultimate Mastery Of Martial Technique (tm), but since each of the first three Forms only requires E2 and any 3 MA Charms, they have a fair bit of value as pseudo-capstones to the other Styles (Four Magical Materials, in particular, has a range of effects to synergize with whatever MA you chose), or to let someone cherry-pick the first Charm each of three different MAs, take this at E2, and feel like they have a &amp;quot;real&amp;quot; Style, with four Charms including a Form.<br /> <br /> So that's my bad. This definitely justifies its place in the book.<br /> <br /> I do need to figure out what degeneracy Soul Fire Shaper allows, however. Ebon Shadow Form has a couple of effects that scale with Essence, though one is problematically locked behind the Terrestrial keyword. Wrathful Winds Roar is as genuinely upsetting as ever (probably 8 levels/dice when you take it, eventually scaling up to 12). I think the real payoff, though, are over in the Anima abilities, many of which scale by Essence. There's tons of &amp;quot;add (essence) bonus successes&amp;quot; stuff, which is gravy, but really this just lets you hit the &amp;quot;dice&amp;quot; limit at E3 rather than E5. The really scary stuff happens if E5 Alchemicals can learn SMA. Lots of them have powerful abilities based on Essence/2 (rounded up), so Soul Fire does all kinds of stupid stuff, like +4 to attack and damage rolls for your whole side. In the land of the canonically supported, Thousand Tears Elixir and the Greater Sign of Secrets both give out some odd results.<br /> <br /> Of course, most of that is a little debatable as being &amp;quot;static value calculations, rolls, or costs,&amp;quot; which I guess is an escape hatch if anything looks too absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless something changed in the newer versions it's still onlu solars-tier beings, sidereals and getimians who can learn it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T12:54:21-07:00","id":1453069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453057#post1453057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereal Active Animas also are mostly converting Essence dice to successes for you and your allies - it's only 1/die per essence for each person, but the area of effect makes it strong, and I don't think caps apply.</div> </div> </div> </div>No reason to think they don't. &quot;If an effect would transform dice into successes, these count towards the success limit,&quot; which is 5. Lesser Signs don't say they avoid the limit (except for the Lesser Sign of Mercury, which oddly is also the only one to add dice instead of converting things into successes), whilst the Adamant and Starmetal abilities do. There's a reason I said it would be pretty outrageous if Alchemicals somehow gained access to Soul Fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453063#post1453063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless something changed in the newer versions it's still onlu solars-tier beings, sidereals and getimians who can learn it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The actual language the book uses is &quot;Terrestrial Exalted typically cannot access these Charms without first undergoing some sort of unusual or extraordinary story event as determined by the Storyteller and player.&quot; That's not really grounds for saying the goofiest interactions I've been able to find are canon - an ST could very easily justify shooting any player down - but it's a lot more permissive than the text of past editions.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, the book doesn't mention Lunars (or other non-SidGet, non-Solaroid Celestials) interacting with Sidereal styles at all. I think it would be a mistake to read much into that, but it's quirky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T13:02:33-07:00","id":1453070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453069#post1453069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The actual language the book uses is &amp;quot;Terrestrial Exalted typically cannot access these Charms without first undergoing some sort of unusual or extraordinary story event as determined by the Storyteller and player.&amp;quot; That's not really grounds for saying the goofiest interactions I've been able to find are canon - an ST could very easily justify shooting any player down - but it's a lot more permissive than the text of past editions.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, the book doesn't mention Lunars (or other non-SidGet, non-Solaroid Celestials) interacting with Sidereal styles at all. I think it would be a mistake to read much into that, but it's quirky.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book by default in the SMA passage before PAoC limits it that way. Without an ST reversing the decision, I assume that's the default. Eric has said there will be a section on what sts can change for PCs but I've never been one for PC exceptionalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T13:11:57-07:00","id":1453071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453069#post1453069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No reason to think they don't. &quot;If an effect would transform dice into successes, these count towards the success limit,&quot; which is 5. Lesser Signs don't say they avoid the limit (except for the Lesser Sign of Mercury, which oddly is also the only one to add dice instead of converting things into successes), whilst the Adamant and Starmetal abilities do. There's a reason I said it would be pretty outrageous if Alchemicals somehow gained access to Soul Fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I missed that.<br /> This makes transforming dice into successes really bad, since it costs you uncapped dice but adds capped successes.<br /> An Essence 10 sidereal actually doesn't gain average successes if you interpret the ability with hostility. Which you shouldn't, but the rules could be harder to be hostile about<br /> And even weirder that Mercury is different - it would have made all Lesser Signs similar except for which rolls they effect, which is part of why I assumed transforming dice to successes was uncapped","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T15:40:35-07:00","id":1453087,"title":"","content":"I don't even know if Essence 10 Sidereals <i>exist</i>. The rules only talk about 1-5, and you master PMoC Style at Essence 3.<br /> <br /> Turning dice into successes is dubious, but might make sense when your allies are using Excellencies, or other dice-adding effects, and not one which add successes. I'd really prefer they just added dice, though - or that the game didn't even have a random assortment of +dice and +success effects, especially with their own separate caps, but what can you do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T06:10:55-07:00","id":1453148,"title":"","content":"The Last preview is out, The Deathlords base template is of course terrifying but not invincible (compared to old school Deathlords). It can easily be translated to quick npcs. More E10 beings than I thought but that's good to know some creatures are still very powerful in the setting.<br /> <br /> The translation chapter/charm design is actually very cool, now it paints a clearer picture of making your own charms.<br /> <br /> Edit: Just noticed a very cool ability, Martial Proficiency, Mortal Masters/Prodigy can use a martial arts charm (the first one) for free once per scene...this actually would make some people happy about Mortal martial artists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2127,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","user":"Eltacolibre","date":". 06-22-2021, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T07:50:45-07:00","id":1453164,"title":"","content":"The Quality rules seems very well designed, I've just created some strong bull god NPC's like Ahlat and they are intuitive to use and seems effective, I'm really happy with them. This is THE feature that 3e was missing for me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T09:02:41-07:00","id":1453171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453148#post1453148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Just noticed a very cool ability, Martial Proficiency, Mortal Masters/Prodigy can use a martial arts charm (the first one) for free once per scene...this actually would make some people happy about Mortal martial artists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was thrilled to see that there. It justifies martial arts as a thing for mortals in setting without being a hugely imbalancing factor. It seems like an elegant way to capture the idea of the &quot;techniques&quot; from early 3e without creating a whole new system. Also, the quality then seems like a reasonable thing for a kung-fu master character to take a venture to add to their disciples.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5849-whiskey-jack","name":"Whiskey Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T11:54:45-07:00","id":1453190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453148#post1453148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Just noticed a very cool ability, Martial Proficiency, Mortal Masters/Prodigy can use a martial arts charm (the first one) for free once per scene...this actually would make some people happy about Mortal martial artists.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's more, now we have a genuine perk to joining the Immaculate Order as a mortal. Imagine, being as fast and nimble as the wind (Air Dragon), able to strike foes down with a single punch (Earth Dragon), draining away your target's energy (Fire Dragon), knowing a specific maneuver to amplify your opponent's pain (Water Dragon), or gaining the ability to track your foes regardless of where they hide (Wood Dragon). When presented with that, it seems easier to imagine a person willing to undertake the vows and restrictions of the Immaculate Order despite not being Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T12:11:31-07:00","id":1453193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Critian Caceorte</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453190#post1453190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's more, now we have a genuine perk to joining the Immaculate Order as a mortal. Imagine, being as fast and nimble as the wind (Air Dragon), able to strike foes down with a single punch (Earth Dragon), draining away your target's energy (Fire Dragon), knowing a specific maneuver to amplify your opponent's pain (Water Dragon), or gaining the ability to track your foes regardless of where they hide (Wood Dragon). When presented with that, it seems easier to imagine a person willing to undertake the vows and restrictions of the Immaculate Order despite not being Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or really any martial society. Things like the golden jannissaries get to exist again as something more than a loose order propped up by a few terrestrial outcastes. Between this and harmonious academic methodology now being a legitimate teaching technique, I can play a ninja grandmaster, inducting dozens of recruits into my ebon shadow society because, while they won't be as spectacular as I am, they won't just be a black pajama squad either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5849-whiskey-jack","name":"Whiskey Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T17:22:26-07:00","id":1453215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453045#post1453045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking back at Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Style, I like it better than I did at first blush.<br /> <br /> Stacking up a ton of scenelongs still doesn't strike me as a very exciting way to convey the Ultimate Mastery Of Martial Technique (tm), but since each of the first three Forms only requires E2 and any 3 MA Charms, they have a fair bit of value as pseudo-capstones to the other Styles (Four Magical Materials, in particular, has a range of effects to synergize with whatever MA you chose), or to let someone cherry-pick the first Charm each of three different MAs, take this at E2, and feel like they have a &quot;real&quot; Style, with four Charms including a Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a note, given establishing most forms are going to be Step 1 charms that cost a mote, and you don't <i>get</i> that many motes in Essence, there is some genuine value to being able to turn on two forms in one turn instead of standing there for three rounds doing nothing but screaming and powering up like a Dragon Ball Z character.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T19:28:28-07:00","id":1453227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453215#post1453215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a note, given establishing most forms are going to be Step 1 charms that cost a mote, and you don't <i>get</i> that many motes in Essence, there is some genuine value to being able to turn on two forms in one turn instead of standing there for three rounds doing nothing but screaming and powering up like a Dragon Ball Z character.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do that already.<br /> <br /> Nothing says that Forms aren't Reflexive Step 1 Charms, so by default, they are. Just flurry two random actions (I favor Full Defense + social influence to Dissuade them, so maybe they have to refuse and give you some dice next turn), and fire a Form at the start of each one. Other than the Super Spirit Bomb, DBZ characters are canonically fighting very fast, gratuitous powerups or no.<br /> <br /> Mote economy is a thing, though. PMoC Form lets you throw up one of the Forms leading into it for 1m committed, instead of 2m. That's a feature, sure, but not the game-changer of getting to mix Forms in past editions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T19:42:53-07:00","id":1453228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453227#post1453227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can do that already.<br /> <br /> Nothing says that Forms aren't Reflexive Step 1 Charms, so by default, they are. Just flurry two random actions (I favor Full Defense + social influence to Dissuade them, so maybe they have to refuse and give you some dice next turn), and fire a Form at the start of each one. Other than the Super Spirit Bomb, DBZ characters are canonically fighting very fast, gratuitous powerups or no.<br /> <br /> Mote economy is a thing, though. PMoC Form lets you throw up one of the Forms leading into it for 1m committed, instead of 2m. That's a feature, sure, but not the game-changer of getting to mix Forms in past editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not, to my recollection, how ExEss charm activation works.<br /> <br /> Forms <i>are</i> Step 1 charms. But there are no combos, if you activate a charm on step 1, that's your lot.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T19:59:20-07:00","id":1453231,"title":"","content":"True. You cannot use any other Step 1 Charm on the same action.<br /> <br /> But a flurry is two actions, so two Step 1s, and there doesn't seem to be any rule that the Charm has anything to do with the action. If a Charm is an action unto itself, it will specify (like a pre-upgrade Glorious Solar Arsenal), and the Forms do not.<br /> <br /> I find this exceedingly odd. I admit I have not gotten confirmation from the writers. But when I asked on the Discord, this was the consensus, and I don't see any rules to contradict it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T21:05:22-07:00","id":1453236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453231#post1453231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. You cannot use any other Step 1 Charm on the same action.<br /> <br /> But a flurry is two actions, so two Step 1s, and there doesn't seem to be any rule that the Charm has anything to do with the action. If a Charm is an action unto itself, it will specify (like a pre-upgrade Glorious Solar Arsenal), and the Forms do not.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be extremely odd to me, given in the core game charms are either an action unto themselves or explicitly supplementing an action; this may be a place where the &quot;simplification&quot; of Essence runs into a problem of clarity. Worth commenting on the feedback form, certainly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T21:15:07-07:00","id":1453238,"title":"","content":"The primary thing I have been talking about, both in the feedback form and around the internet, is places where the simplification of Essence run into problems with clarity.<br /> <br /> Not unrelatedly, the main thing which still has me debating how much I want this is trying to parse from the Devs' responses how much editing will take place to improve that clarity.<br /> <br /> I will level with you: I honestly do not have a reasonable guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T04:13:10-07:00","id":1453257,"title":"","content":"Excellencies and the Action Order<br /> <br /> Out of combat, you can use whatever Charms make sense. If I get to roll Integrity to resist a Deathlord, I can do that with an Excellency. If I have to resist an environmental hazard, I can use an Excellency.<br /> <br /> But what about in combat?<br /> <br /> In combat, I'm limited to one Charm per step. Excellencies are Step 1.<br /> <br /> In combat, if I'm trapped in a burning building, can I use an Excellency on my roll to resist?<br /> <br /> I don't think I can. <br /> <br /> I can roll to resist, but I don't get a Step 1 because I'm not declaring an action, I'm defending, so no Excellency? Like if I use Flickering Shadow Evasion to defend against an attack, I can roll (Attribute + Athletics) to defend against an attack, but I can't use the Excellency on that roll.<br /> <br /> Or is this another case of simplification butting against clarity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T04:58:50-07:00","id":1453261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453257#post1453257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellencies and the Action Order<br /> <br /> Out of combat, you can use whatever Charms make sense. If I get to roll Integrity to resist a Deathlord, I can do that with an Excellency. If I have to resist an environmental hazard, I can use an Excellency.<br /> <br /> But what about in combat?<br /> <br /> In combat, I'm limited to one Charm per step. Excellencies are Step 1.<br /> <br /> In combat, if I'm trapped in a burning building, can I use an Excellency on my roll to resist?<br /> <br /> I don't think I can.<br /> <br /> I can roll to resist, but I don't get a Step 1 because I'm not declaring an action, I'm defending, so no Excellency? Like if I use Flickering Shadow Evasion to defend against an attack, I can roll (Attribute + Athletics) to defend against an attack, but I can't use the Excellency on that roll.<br /> <br /> Or is this another case of simplification butting against clarity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I can't say, but I would tend to say that you can use Charms like Excellencies for defending &quot;non-combat effects&quot; during combat, as long as it doesn't create new actions on your round (or else it's submitted to the Number of Actions per round restriction)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T05:34:12-07:00","id":1453264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453261#post1453261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charms like Excellencies</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that's just fuzzier to me. I'm fighting someone using Volcano Cutter, they make a lava hazard under me.<br /> <br /> Do I get to reflexively activate Earth Dragon Form (to remove wound penalties), use the Athletics Excellency (to add five bonus dice to resist the lava), and take Air Dragon Form as well (for the bonus success in avoiding the lava)?<br /> <br /> Because out of combat, that's going all out to get past a hazard... but in combat... I just got two scene long charms up and can Excellency my next attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-23-2021, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T06:53:31-07:00","id":1453269,"title":"","content":"Also - you definitely can activate charms on steps 2 and 8 and probably some other steps of attacks against you, otherwise defensive charms wouldn't work.<br /> You can also activate charms on step 2 of attacks against other people, otherwise the reflexive defend other charms wouldn't work.<br /> Nothing in the rules implies attacks are special in terms of this except for what steps they have, so you possibly can activate charms in any action anyone in the scene takes.<br /> Nothing in the rules says steps 2 and 8 and whatever are special. The description of the steps makes those the relatively target-facing rather than actor-facing steps, but it doesn't clearly say &quot;here are the steps where the actor uses charms, here are the steps where other people use charms&quot; at any point in the rules I remember reading.<br /> Nothing in the rules states those charms are special, except insofar as they specify which steps and which kinds of actions they're activated on.<br /> <br /> So, it looks to me like it's possible to activate a form charm on step 1 of literally any action in a fight.<br /> <br /> This clearly isn't the intent, but I have no idea how we're supposed to figure out the intent from what's written. Form charms can offer defensive boosts, so it's reasonable to want to activate them on step 1 of an attack against you, or an attack you're defending other against, or that you're going to defend other against, but maybe you can't? You almost certainly shouldn't be able to activate them on step 1 of someone trying to convince someone else to do something, but I don't see any rule actually drawing a distinction between those.<br /> <br /> There's so little guidance on when charms can be activated, in the face of a fairly strict and arbitrary rule limiting when they can be activated.<br /> <br /> Flow like Blood is another good charm to think about in this context. It doesn't say what step it's activated on, so it defaults to step 1. It's a defensive charm, so you're likely to want to activate it on someone else's attack. Can you, or do you need to activate it on step 1 of your own action?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23597,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","user":"autXautY","date":". 06-23-2021, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T07:05:28-07:00","id":1453270,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not a dev but one of them confirmed that Step 1 only exists for your own non-defensive actions. So you could have two Step 1s in a round if you flurried or used a counterattack effect.<br /> <br /> So, no, Excellencies can\u2019t be used defensively in combat, as-written, and form Charms can be used at the start of unrelated actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 06-23-2021, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T07:31:14-07:00","id":1453272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453270#post1453270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not a dev but one of them confirmed that Step 1 only exists for your own non-defensive actions. So you could have two Step 1s in a round if you flurried or used a counterattack effect.<br /> <br /> So, no, Excellencies can\u2019t be used defensively in combat, as-written, and form Charms can be used at the start of unrelated actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>OTOH, the Excellencies themselves explain how they work with static values, and those are used only on defensive actions. So the rules are at odds with themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T08:10:49-07:00","id":1453280,"title":"","content":"Can't you use your Excellency on someone else's Step 1 in increase your static values?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T08:26:47-07:00","id":1453285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453280#post1453280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't you use your Excellency on someone else's Step 1 in increase your static values?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would not appear so. &quot;<i>Outside of combat</i>, this may be used to boost passive values.&quot; Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> In other words, you can use the Excellency to boost passive values, just not in combat, because combat has Steps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 06-23-2021, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T08:32:07-07:00","id":1453286,"title":"","content":"Ah, true. I forgot about it only working for that outside of combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T17:44:44-07:00","id":1453420,"title":"","content":"I have yet to see a dev clarification for the confusion about how simple actions and charms work if they are not a typical attack (withering, decisive, gambit) or social influence action. This is the single biggest system issue / confusion I have, so if I want to use Essence right now I need to decide how I want to handle it at my table. What I've come up with is: Attack actions use the 8-step process, with one charm per step as per the RAW, so Excellency can't be used on step 2. Social actions are RAW with 4 steps. Other simple actions that don't have an explicit structure of steps (like build power, miscellaneous actions like picking a lock, etc.) are just treated as non-combat actions so any one charm can be used, ignoring step restrictions. <br /> <br /> Regarding defending against the environmental hazard from Volcano Cutter, my reading is that the wielder of the artifact uses their action and the evocation to create the environmental hazard, but it isn't an attack (ie, not withering or decisive) and the hazard damage isn't something that takes place within the step structure of the enemy's turn. They declare their action on step 1 but you aren't defending against it on a step 2 or anything. They just create the hazard and that is their action and their turn ends. Then the hazard takes over and affects the people in the area once per turn on their turn, and the character responds to that situation with a reflexive action at that point. So I think RAW is that you can use an Excellency to avoid that hazard, since the hazard damage is not occurring during some step of the enemy's action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26886-lindharin","name":"Lindharin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T17:51:37-07:00","id":1453421,"title":"","content":"There is one RAW case where you can use Excellency to defend against an attack, at least sort of. You can always choose to Clash against an attack. Instead of letting them attack on Step 1 and you use a Defense at step 2, it spins off an alternate structure where you both attack using Steps 1 and 3 (no one uses steps 2 and 4), and the highest attack wins. That way both of you can use an Excellency. Obviously limited since it consumes your next turn's action, but it can be a useful high risk/high reward option. And in some cases, it might be a safer option to relying on your Defense against some types of attacks - someone with a middle-range attack pool but a very large damage pool would be a great foe to clash against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26886-lindharin","name":"Lindharin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T20:11:50-07:00","id":1453430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lindharin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453421#post1453421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is one RAW case where you can use Excellency to defend against an attack, at least sort of. You can always choose to Clash against an attack. Instead of letting them attack on Step 1 and you use a Defense at step 2, it spins off an alternate structure where you both attack using Steps 1 and 3 (no one uses steps 2 and 4), and the highest attack wins. That way both of you can use an Excellency. Obviously limited since it consumes your next turn's action, but it can be a useful high risk/high reward option. And in some cases, it might be a safer option to relying on your Defense against some types of attacks - someone with a middle-range attack pool but a very large damage pool would be a great foe to clash against.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure this works, actually. I think you can only enhance clashes with Charms that specifically state as much, and the Excellency doesn't have that clause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-24T20:31:33-07:00","id":1453431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1452119-let-s-talk-about-the-charms-of-exess?p=1453430#post1453430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure this works, actually. I think you can only enhance clashes with Charms that specifically state as much, and the Excellency doesn't have that clause.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch and interesting point. Well, it lets you negate the enemy's use of an Excellency then; both of you are in the same boat at that point. Need to think about that a little more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26886-lindharin","name":"Lindharin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}